    <node id="AEROMONAS SP.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Aeromonas sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts that can grow on polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Aeromonas sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms and superworms, capable of degrading plastics like polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Aeromonas sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms and superworms, capable of growing on polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Aeromonas sp. is a symbiotic bacterium isolated from mealworms that contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLEBSIELLA PNEUMONIAE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworm guts that can grow on polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms and superworms, capable of degrading plastics like polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella pneumoniae is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms and superworms, capable of growing on polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella pneumoniae is a species of bacteria in the gut microbiome of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella pneumoniae is a nitrogen-fixing bacterium found in the gut of termites, contributing to nitrogen metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella pneumoniae is a symbiotic bacterium isolated from mealworms that has been shown to degrade polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XPS SPECTRA">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">XPS spectra analysis is used to study the chemical structure of polymers, such as polyether-PU foam, before and after degradation by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUT MICROBIAL COMMUNITIES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Gut microbial communities in Tenebrio larvae, including specific bacterial families, play a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene and other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbial communities in mealworms and Indianmeal moth larvae play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics by breaking down complex polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbial communities in mealworms and Indianmeal moth larvae play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics by breaking down complex polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbial communities refer to the collective populations of bacteria and fungi in the digestive tract of insect larvae, which play a significant role in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial communities of mealworms consist of various bacterial families that shift in composition based on diet, particularly when consuming polyether-PU foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbial communities refer to the diverse microorganisms living in the digestive tracts of organisms, such as bumble bees, which can influence health and disease resistance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALPHA DIVERSITY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Alpha diversity analysis measures the species richness and evenness of microbial communities, such as those in the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha diversity measures the complexity of gut bacterial species diversity in larvae, calculated using indices such as Chao1 and Shannon.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha diversity measures the complexity of gut bacterial species diversity in larvae, calculated using indices such as Chao1 and Shannon.&lt;SEP&gt;Alpha diversity measures the species diversity in the mealworm gut microbiome, which remains stable despite changes in diet, such as the inclusion of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRINCIPAL COORDINATE ANALYSIS (PCOA)">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to analyze the differences in gut microbiome composition between bran-fed and PU-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis is a statistical method used to analyze shifts in gut microbial community structure in Tenebrio molitor larvae during plastic biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis is a statistical method used to visualize differences in microbial communities based on diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to investigate changes in the microbial community structure of T. obscurus and T. molitor when fed polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms under different feeding conditions, providing insights into microbial community structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to compare the gut microbial communities of mealworms fed different diets, revealing distinct clusters based on molecular weight of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
