    <node id="INDIAN MEALMOTH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Indian mealmoth larvae are known to host Enterobacter asburiae YT1, a bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Indian mealmoth larvae are organisms from which Enterobacter sp., a bacterium capable of degrading low-density polyethylene (LDPE), was isolated.&lt;SEP&gt;Indian mealmoths (Plodia interpunctella) are larvae capable of ingesting and biodegrading polyethylene.</data>
