    <node id="STAPHYLOCOCCUS SP.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterial genus associated with the gut microbiome of polyether-PU-fed mealworms, potentially involved in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Staphylococcus sp. is a gut bacterium found in mealworms that plays a role in the degradation of both polystyrene and corn straw.&lt;SEP&gt;Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterial genus studied for its role in the biodegradation of polystyrene styrofoam in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterial species associated with the biodegradation of polyethylene.</data>
