    <node id="PRINCIPAL COORDINATE ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Principal Coordinate Analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to visualize differences in microbial communities, such as those in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Principal coordinate analysis (PCoA) is a statistical method used to visualize and interpret complex data, such as microbial communities involved in biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPE">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Scanning Electron Microscope (SEM) is an imaging technique used to study the surface morphology of materials, including plastics undergoing biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning electron microscope (SEM) is a tool used to study the surface morphology of materials, including microplastics and nanoplastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THERMOGRAVIMETRIC ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Thermogravimetric Analysis (TGA) is a method used to study the thermal stability and decomposition of polymers, including those degraded by microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric analysis is used to study the thermal degradation of microplastics and frass, revealing changes in weight loss stages and decomposition rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric Analysis (TGA) is a technique used to assess the thermostability and degradation of polypropylene materials in the frass of yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermogravimetric analysis (TGA) is a technique used to study the thermal stability and decomposition of materials, including plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TOLUENE 2,4-DIISOCYANATE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Toluene 2,4-diisocyanate (TDI) is a chemical used in the production of polyurethane, studied for its environmental and health impacts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TETRAHYDROFURAN">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent commonly used in polymer chemistry and plastic analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used in polymer research, including studies on the degradation of plastics like polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to dissolve PVC and frass specimens for analysis in gel permeation chromatography (GPC).&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to stop biological activity in biodegradation experiments involving homogenate paste and plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran is a solvent used for extracting polystyrene from mealworm frass samples during the characterization of plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is an organic solvent used in polymer processing and chemical reactions, often involved in plastic extraction and analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="X-RAY PHOTOELECTRON SPECTROSCOPY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy (XPS) is a surface-sensitive technique used to analyze the chemical composition of materials, including degraded plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy is used to analyze the surface chemical components of polystyrene films after bacterial degradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMAMONAS ACIDOVORANS TB-35">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Comamonas acidovorans TB-35 is a bacterial strain known for its ability to degrade polyester urethane, contributing to plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ASPERGILLUS TUBINGENSIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Aspergillus tubingenis is a fungal strain isolated from soil, known for its ability to degrade polyurethane (PU).&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungal species studied for its ability to degrade polyester polystyrene, offering potential solutions for plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus capable of biodegrading polyester polystyrene, contributing to environmental pollution mitigation.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus capable of biodegrading polyester polyurethane, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus capable of biodegrading polyester polyurethane, contributing to the reduction of environmental pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Aspergillus tubingensis is a fungus capable of biodegrading polyester polyurethane, contributing to environmental remediation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BACILLUS SP. YP1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">**Bacillus sp. YP1** is a bacterial strain primarily isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms (*Plodia interpunctella* larvae), although it has also been found in darkling beetles and mealworms. This bacterium is renowned for its ability to degrade polyethylene (PE), particularly low-density polyethylene (LDPE), a common type of plastic. The strain has been extensively studied for its role in plastic degradation, with a strong emphasis on its capacity to break down polyethylene, a polymer similar in structure to polystyrene. While some sources mention its potential role in degrading polystyrene, this feature is less prominent compared to its polyethylene-degrading capabilities.

**Bacillus sp. YP1** has demonstrated higher efficiency in degrading LDPE films compared to other bacterial isolates, making it a significant player in environmental biotechnology and plastic waste management. Its discovery in the gut of waxworms highlights the potential of gut-associated bacteria in addressing plastic pollution. Overall, **Bacillus sp. YP1** is a key microbial strain in the biodegradation of plastics, particularly polyethylene, and continues to be a focus of research in the field of plastic degradation studies. The strain's ability to degrade polyethylene underscores the potential of microorganisms in managing plastic waste, contributing to advancements in environmental sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENTEROBACTER ASBURIAE VT1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">**Enterobacter asburiae VT1** is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms, specifically those capable of consuming polyethylene (PE). This strain is notable for its ability to degrade polyethylene, contributing significantly to the biodegradation of plastic. The discovery of Enterobacter asburiae VT1 highlights the role of gut bacteria in plastic degradation, particularly in waxworms that feed on polyethylene. The strain has been consistently identified as a key player in the breakdown of polyethylene, underscoring its potential in addressing plastic pollution through microbial biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms, known for its ability to degrade polyethylene (PE).&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is another bacterial strain isolated from the guts of plastic-eating waxworms, contributing to polyethylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from plastic-eating waxworms that can degrade polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae strain VT1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterium isolated from waxworm guts, playing a role in plastic waste degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms, capable of degrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of plastic-eating waxworms, capable of degrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is another bacterial strain isolated from waxworms, involved in polyethylene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is a bacterial strain isolated from waxworms, involved in the degradation of polyethylene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47</data>
