    <node id="ENTEROBACTER SP. D1">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of Galleria mellonella, capable of biodegrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of Galleria mellonella, known for its ability to biodegrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) that can biodegrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) that can biodegrade polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the gut microbiome of insects, contributing to the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae, capable of biodegrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain isolated from the guts of wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) that can degrade polyethylene.</data>
