    <node id="POLYESTER POLYURETHANE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyester polyurethane is a plastic material that can be biodegraded by microorganisms like Aspergillus sp. S45 and Pseudomonas aeruginosa.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyester polyurethane is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by fungi like Aspergillus tubingensis.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyester polyurethane is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain fungi, such as Aspergillus tubingensis, reducing its environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyester polyurethane is a type of polyurethane that can be degraded by certain fungi, contributing to biodegradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyester polyurethane is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by microorganisms such as Aspergillus tubingensis.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyester polyurethane is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, such as Cladosporium sp. P7.</data>
