    <node id="PLANCTOMYCETES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Planctomycetes are a group of bacteria found in the ocean that are involved in nitrogen fixation, contributing to marine ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Planctomycetes are bacteria that have mechanisms for nitrogen fixation and ammonia oxidation, facilitating nitrogen uptake by larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Planctomycetes is a bacterial phylum found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, showing higher proportions in the polystyrene-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Planctomycetes is a phylum of bacteria that increased in abundance in the gut microbiome of mealworms after feeding on polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Planctomycetes is a bacterial phylum found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, showing higher proportions in the polystyrene-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Planctomycetes is a phylum of bacteria that increased in abundance in the gut microbiome of mealworms after feeding on polystyrene.</data>
