      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrospirae is a bacterial phylum in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions observed in the polystyrene-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrospirae is a bacterial phylum in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions observed in the polystyrene-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrospirae is a phylum of bacteria that includes Nitrosospira, which are involved in nitrogen cycling and organic matter degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrospirae is a phylum of bacteria that increased in the gut microbiome of mealworms after feeding on polystyrene, indicating a potential role in anaerobic processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrospirae is a phylum of bacteria that includes Nitrosospira, which are involved in nitrogen cycling and organic matter degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrospirae is a phylum of bacteria that increased in the gut microbiome of mealworms after feeding on polystyrene, indicating a potential role in anaerobic processes.</data>
