    <node id="CARDBOARD">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Cardboard (CEL) is a substrate used in studies to assess its impact on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard (CEL) is a substrate used in studies to assess its impact on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a cellulose-based material that may serve as a substrate for microbial degradation processes, including plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a cellulose-based material used as one of the substrates in the study to evaluate mealworm digestion capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a dietary variant used in experiments to study the enzymatic activity in the digestive tracts of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a substrate fed to mealworm larvae to study its impact on microbial diversity and biodegradation efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a feed type used in the study to compare the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is used as a diet for mealworms, affecting their microbiome and biochemical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is used as a diet in the study, showing less favorable effects on the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae compared to other diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is used as a reference substrate in the study to compare its effects on mealworm larvae growth and waste degradation with plastic substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a material used to feed mealworms before experiments, containing natural fibers from sources like sugarcane and bamboo.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a cellulose-based material that may serve as a substrate for microbial degradation processes, including plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a cellulose-based material used as one of the substrates in the study to evaluate mealworm digestion capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a material studied in the context of mealworm digestion, where it influences the enzymatic activity of their digestive tracts and symbiotic bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Cardboard is a substrate fed to mealworm larvae to study its impact on microbial diversity and biodegradation efficiency.</data>
