    <node id="OXO-DEGRADABLE POLYETHYLENE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Oxo-degradable polyethylene (PE-oxo) is a type of plastic used as a substrate in studies to evaluate its effects on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene (PE-oxo) is a type of plastic used as a substrate in studies to evaluate its effects on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of plastic that degrades through oxidation and is used in experiments to study enzymatic activity in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of polyethylene designed to degrade more quickly under environmental conditions, used as a substrate in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of plastic that may form toxic byproducts when degraded in the digestive system of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of plastic used as a feed type in the study to assess its impact on Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of synthetic polymer that mealworms can consume, affecting their survival and growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of plastic that degrades through oxidation and is being studied in the context of mealworm digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxo-degradable polyethylene is a type of polyethylene designed to degrade more quickly under environmental conditions, used as a substrate in the study.</data>
