      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Polyethylene regranulate (PE-reg) is a recycled plastic used as a substrate in studies to assess its impact on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate (PE-reg) is a recycled plastic used as a substrate in studies to assess its impact on the gut microbiome of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a recycled form of polyethylene used as a substrate in the study to assess mealworm digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a recycled form of polyethylene used in experiments to study enzymatic activity in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a recycled form of polyethylene used in mealworm diets, influencing their microbiome and biochemical properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a type of plastic used as a feed type in the study to assess its impact on Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a recycled form of polyethylene used as a substrate in the study to assess mealworm digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene regranulate is a recycled form of polyethylene, which is being investigated for its interaction with mealworm digestive enzymes.</data>
