    <node id="SHANNON DIVERSITY INDEX">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The Shannon diversity index is a measure used to assess the diversity of the mealworm gut microbiome under different diets, such as PU and bran.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shannon diversity index is used to measure the species diversity of microorganisms in the digestive tracts of mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shannon diversity index was used to represent the alpha diversity of the gut microbiome in larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shannon diversity index is used to measure the species diversity of microorganisms in the digestive tracts of mealworm larvae.</data>
