    <node id="ALPHAPROTEOBACTERIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Alphaproteobacteria is a bacterial class present in the gut microbiota of Alphitobius diaperinus, though in smaller proportions, it may still contribute to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria found in the gut microbiota of mealworms, particularly in the PS diet group, indicating a role in nitrogen metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria present in the gut microbiome of mealworms, involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a dominant bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions in oatmeal waste and cardboard-fed variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria represented by one strain in the study, potentially involved in the degradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a class of bacteria that includes one strain isolated from mealworms, which is capable of degrading polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alphaproteobacteria is a dominant bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions in oatmeal waste and cardboard-fed variants.</data>
