    </node>
    <node id="CLOSTRIDIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Clostridia is a bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions in the oatmeal waste-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with higher proportions in the oatmeal waste-fed variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a class of anaerobic bacteria within the Firmicutes phylum, contributing to the gut microbiota of mealworms and polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridia is a class of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
