    <node id="FLAVOBACTERIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Flavobacteria is a bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, present across all feeding variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Flavobacteria is a bacterial class in the gut microbiome of mealworms, present across all feeding variants.&lt;SEP&gt;Flavobacteria is a class of bacteria that includes Flavobacterium and Chryseobacterium, which are involved in the degradation of organic matter.&lt;SEP&gt;Flavobacteria is a class of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, playing a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Flavobacteria is a class of bacteria that includes Flavobacterium and Chryseobacterium, which are involved in the degradation of organic matter.</data>
