    <node id="TENERICUTES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Tenericutes is a dominant phylum in the gut bacterial communities of yellow mealworms fed with PP, indicating its potential role in PP degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a dominant phylum in the gut bacterial community of PE-fed yellow mealworms, suggesting its involvement in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria that includes Mollicutes, which are known for their role in various environmental processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria present in the gut microbiota of mealworms, contributing to the microbial community involved in polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria found in the gut of mealworms and is linked to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a dominant phylum in the mealworm gut microbiome, observed in both PU and bran diets, and plays a role in digestion and plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a dominant phylum in the gut microbiome of yellow mealworms, particularly in PP-fed groups, indicating a shift in bacterial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria that is part of the gut microbial community in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenericutes is a phylum of bacteria that includes Mollicutes, which are known for their role in various environmental processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALKALINE PHOSPHATASE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of phosphorus bonds and is correlated with the degradation of polystyrene in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that plays a role in the breakdown of organic compounds, including those found in plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that catalyzes the breakdown of phosphorus bonds and is highly active in the digestive tracts of mealworms, particularly in the presence of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkaline phosphatase is an enzyme that plays a role in the breakdown of organic compounds, including those found in plastics.</data>
