      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterococcus is a genus of Lactobacillales that may play a role in the degradation of organic compounds, including plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus is a genus of Lactobacillales that may play a role in the degradation of organic compounds, including plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, including species like Enterococcus faecium and Enterococcus mundtii.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiota of insect larvae, which may contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
