    <node id="SPIROPLASMA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Spiroplasma is a genus of Mollicutes that may contribute to the degradation of organic materials, including plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria belonging to the Mollicutes class within the Tenericutes phylum. It is predominantly found in the gut microbiome of mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) and other insect larvae, such as superworms. Spiroplasma is strongly associated with the degradation of various plastics, including polyethylene (PE), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), polypropylene (PP), and polystyrene (PS), as well as lignocellulose and other organic materials. This genus is particularly abundant in the gut microbiota of mealworms fed with normal diets (e.g., bran) compared to those fed with specific plastics like PS and low-density polyethylene (LDPE). However, it also shows increased abundance in larvae fed with PP and PS, suggesting its potential role in the biodegradation of these materials.

While Spiroplasma is known to be pathogenic in some insect species, it does not harm Tenebrio molitor larvae. Instead, it plays a significant role in digestion and plastic degradation within their gut microbiome. Its dominance in the gut microbiota of mealworms, especially those fed with PP foam plastics, highlights its potential as a key player in the biodegradation of synthetic polymers. Overall, Spiroplasma is a versatile and ecologically important bacterium in the gut microbiome of mealworms, contributing to both digestion and the breakdown of challenging environmental pollutants like plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria that can be associated with the gut microbiota of organisms involved in biodegradation studies.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896</data>
