    <node id="ENZYME ACTIVITY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Enzyme activity refers to the study of how enzymes produced by mealworm digestive tracts and their symbiotic bacteria interact with various materials, including plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzyme activity was a key focus of the study, with measurements taken across different diets and experimental conditions to assess variations in the digestive tract and bacterial communities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3ce1f7a057da80b206f8354c70d120c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </node>
    <node id="C8 ESTERASE LIPASE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">C8 esterase lipase is an enzyme that shows elevated activity in the presence of polyethylene regranulate and is correlated with polystyrene degradation in mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SYMBIOTIC BACTERIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Symbiotic bacteria are microorganisms isolated from the gut of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic bacteria are microorganisms that live in a mutually beneficial relationship with their host, such as nitrogen-fixing bacteria in the guts of insects.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic bacteria in the digestive tracts of mealworms play a crucial role in the enzymatic degradation of materials like polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic bacteria in the gut of insects, such as Tenebrio molitor, play a role in nitrogen fixation and the degradation of polymer wastes.&lt;SEP&gt;Symbiotic bacteria in the digestive tracts of mealworms play a crucial role in enzyme production and the degradation of materials such as plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1</data>
    </node>
