    <node id="PHOSPHORUS BONDS">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Phosphorus bonds are chemical bonds broken down by enzymes such as alkaline phosphatase and acid phosphatase, which are highly active in mealworm digestive tracts.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus bonds are chemical bonds that are broken down by enzymes like alkaline phosphatase and acid phosphatase, which are active in the digestive tracts of mealworms.</data>
