      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Organic phosphorus compounds are transformed into inorganic soluble phosphates by enzymes in the digestive tracts of mealworms, making them available for living organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INORGANIC SOLUBLE PHOSPHATES">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Inorganic soluble phosphates are the end products of the breakdown of organic phosphorus compounds by enzymes in the digestive tracts of mealworms.</data>
