      <data key="d1">Spiroplasma spp. are bacteria predominantly found in mealworm larvae fed bran, polystyrene, and polyethylene, playing a role in their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Spiroplasma spp. are predominant bacterial taxa found in mealworm larvae fed bran, polystyrene, and polyethylene, playing a role in the gut microbiome.</data>
