      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Citrobacter spp. are bacteria belonging to the Proteobacteria phylum and are known potential nitrogen-fixing bacteria found in the gut of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrobacter spp. are bacteria that colonize mealworm larvae fed both polystyrene and polyethylene, playing a role in the degradation of these polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Citrobacter spp. are bacteria that colonize mealworm larvae fed polystyrene and polyethylene, contributing to their gut microbiome.</data>
