    <node id="NITROSIRA DEFLUVI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrosira defluvii is a bacterium found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, suggesting a mixotrophic lifestyle and involvement in nitrogen metabolism during polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrosira defluvii is a bacterium whose proportion increases in mealworm larvae fed polystyrene-based diets, indicating its role in polymer degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrosira defluvii is a bacterium that increases in proportion in mealworm larvae fed polystyrene-based diets.</data>
