    </node>
    <node id="CLOSTRIDIUM SPP.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Clostridium spp. are anaerobic bacteria in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae that play a role in the degradation of hemicellulose and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium spp. are anaerobic bacteria in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae that decompose hemicellulose and polyethylene under natural conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium spp. are bacteria that predominantly colonize mealworm larvae fed bran, contributing to the gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium spp. are bacteria that are part of the gut microbiome and are involved in various metabolic processes, including nitrogen metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium spp. are bacteria predominantly found in mealworm larvae fed bran, contributing to their gut microbiome.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </node>
