    <node id="RHODOCOCCUS SP.">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial genus studied for its role in the biodegradation of polystyrene styrofoam in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from mangrove sediment, known for its ability to degrade polypropylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a species of Actinobacteria that supplies insects with amino acids and is found in the digestive tract of insects like Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. strain CS is a bacterial strain involved in the biodegradation of environmental pollutants, particularly hydrocarbons.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a gut bacterium found in mealworms that is involved in the degradation of both polystyrene and corn straw.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from mangrove sediment, involved in the biodegradation of polypropylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from mangrove sediment, involved in the biodegradation of polypropylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhodococcus sp. is a genus of Actinobacteria that supplies insects with amino acids and is found in their digestive tracts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SPIROCHAETES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Spirochaetes are bacteria found in the digestive tract of termites, responsible for cellulose degradation, nitrogen cycling, and nutrient supply.&lt;SEP&gt;Spirochaetes are bacteria responsible for cellulose degradation and nitrogen cycling in the digestive tracts of insects like termites.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
