    <node id="ACIDOBACTERIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Acidobacteria are bacteria found in the digestive tract of termites, responsible for cellulose degradation and nutrient supply.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidobacteria is a class of bacteria present in the gut microbiome of mealworms, playing a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidobacteria is a minor phylum detected in the gut microbiome of mealworms, with a low percentage presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Acidobacteria are bacteria involved in nutrient cycling and fermentation in the digestive tracts of insects.</data>
