    <node id="WOLBACHIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria that can act as a symbiont in insects, potentially influencing nitrogen metabolism and survival in nutrient-deficient environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria that can enter into symbiotic relationships with insects, influencing their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Wolbachia is a genus of bacteria that forms symbiotic relationships with insects, influencing their reproductive processes.</data>
