    <node id="ENTOMOPLASMATALES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Entomoplasmatales are bacteria found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly associated with polyethylene-based diets, and may play a role in synthetic waste degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is a class of bacteria commonly found in the digestive systems of insects, including mealworms, and is associated with pathogenic processes in the PE-oxo diet group.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that can enter into symbiotic relationships with insects, influencing their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that is significantly more abundant in the PE-oxo variant of the gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria with an average abundance of 1.1% in the gut microbiome, showing significantly higher levels in the PE-oxo variant.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria identified in the gut microbiome of insects, potentially involved in nitrogen metabolism and waste degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that form symbiotic relationships with insects, contributing to their gut microbiome.</data>
