    <node id="NITROGENASE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogenase is an enzyme involved in nitrogen fixation, which is repressed by the availability of nitrogen in the diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogenase is an enzyme produced by symbiotic bacteria that facilitates nitrogen fixation, dependent on trace elements like iron, sulfur, vanadium, and manganese.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogenase is an enzyme produced by symbiotic bacteria that facilitates nitrogen fixation, enabling insects to survive in nitrogen-deficient environments.</data>
