      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Esterase is an enzyme produced by bacterial strains such as Pseudomonas aeruginosa M2 and Achromobacter xylosidans M9, contributing to polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterase is an enzyme whose activity increases in Tenebrio molitor larvae fed polyethylene, indicating its role in polymer degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Esterase is an enzyme whose activity increases in Tenebrio molitor larvae fed polyethylene, indicating its role in polymer degradation.</data>
