    <node id="NEXT-GENERATION SEQUENCING">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Next-generation sequencing is a method used to explore the gut microbiome of mealworms and investigate the effect of PS diets on microbial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing is a technique used to identify bacterial groups involved in waste degradation in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing is a technique used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms and its changes under different plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing was used to analyze the gut microbiome of insect larvae and identify key bacterial species involved in polypropylene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Next-generation sequencing is a technique used to identify bacterial groups in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae that participate in waste degradation.</data>
