    </node>
    <node id="TERMITE GROUP 1 BACTERIA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Termite Group 1 bacteria are uncultured bacteria found in the gut of termites, contributing to nitrogen fixation and coevolution with their host.&lt;SEP&gt;Termite Group 1 bacteria are uncultured bacteria found in the guts of termites, contributing to the coevolution of gut microbiota and termite hosts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">STYROFOAM, a trade name for expanded polystyrene (EPS or PS), is a lightweight polymer widely used in packaging, insulation, and food packaging. Despite its practical applications, STYROFOAM is a significant environmental pollutant due to its non-biodegradable nature under normal conditions. Its resistance to degradation leads to long-term environmental challenges, earning it the label of a "white pollutant." The material's persistence in the environment and its fragmentation into microplastics and nanoplastics exacerbate its ecological impact, posing threats to wildlife and human health. Additionally, its low recycling rate makes it a major contributor to plastic debris.

Recent research has revealed that certain organisms, such as mealworms (Tenebrio molitor), superworms (Zophobas morio), and greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella), can consume and biodegrade STYROFOAM. Mealworm larvae, in particular, have been shown to break down the material in their gut, transforming it into carbon dioxide and potentially using it as an energy source. However, the consumption of STYROFOAM by mealworms has been observed to affect their growth and reproduction. The gut microbiota of these insects, along with certain bacterial strains, play a key role in the biodegradation process. This discovery highlights the potential for biological solutions to mitigate the environmental impact of STYROFOAM, with efforts exploring its use as a feed source for these insects as a promising avenue for reducing plastic waste.

Despite these advancements, STYROFOAM remains a major environmental concern due to its slow degradation and widespread use. Its persistence in the environment and role as a major plastic debris emphasize the urgency of finding effective methods to reduce its ecological footprint. Continued research and innovative solutions are essential to manage its impact on ecosystems and address the challenges posed by this persistent pollutant.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767