    <node id="PLASTIC DEBRIS">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plastic debris refers to discarded plastic materials that accumulate in the environment, causing pollution and harm to ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to larger pieces of plastic waste that break down into microplastics, contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to plastic waste that accumulates in the environment, particularly in marine ecosystems, posing threats to wildlife and ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to fragments of plastic materials, such as polystyrene and polyurethane, that are derived from larvae gnawing and are studied for their environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to plastic waste found in the environment, particularly in oceans, posing significant ecological threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to discarded plastic materials that accumulate in the environment, particularly in marine ecosystems, causing pollution and harm to wildlife.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic debris refers to plastic waste found in the environment, which poses significant threats to ecosystems and organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUT MICROBIOTAASSAY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
