    <node id="MARINE ENVIRONMENT">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">The marine environment is a critical ecosystem that is increasingly polluted by microplastics and other contaminants, requiring extensive research for identification and quantification.&lt;SEP&gt;The marine environment is impacted by polystyrene pollution, which affects marine ecosystems and organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The marine environment is threatened by drifting polymeric materials, such as plastic debris, which harm marine life and ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;The marine environment is a significant area where plastic polymers degrade, contributing to microplastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The marine environment is threatened by drifting polymeric materials, such as plastics, which pose significant ecological risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DRIFTING POLYMERIC MATERIALS">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Drifting polymeric materials are plastic waste that pollute marine environments, posing significant ecological threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Drifting polymeric materials, including plastics, are pollutants that threaten marine ecosystems due to their persistence and harmful effects.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
