      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gut Microbiotassay is a high-throughput qPCR approach combined with next-generation sequencing to study gut microbial diversity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gut Microbiotassay is a high-throughput qPCR method combined with next-generation sequencing to study gut microbial diversity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NITROGEN-FIXING COMMUNITY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">The nitrogen-fixing community in termite guts is shaped by ectosymbiotic bacteria, aiding in nutrient cycling.&lt;SEP&gt;The nitrogen-fixing community in termites consists of microorganisms that play a role in converting nitrogen into a usable form for the host.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
