    <node id="ENTEROBACTER">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria associated with the degradation of polypropylene (PP) in the guts of superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of insect larvae, associated with the degradation of polypropylene (PP) plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, contributing to their digestive processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria predominant in the gut microbiome of mealworms, contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria found in the mealworm gut microbiome, showing significant differences in abundance between feeding groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of mealworms, aiding in digestion and gut health.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of bacteria found in the guts of greater wax moth larvae, associated with polystyrene digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter is a genus of gut microorganisms identified in insect larvae, contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
