      <data key="d1">Kluyvera is a bacterial genus predominant in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae during polypropylene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a genus of bacteria associated with the degradation of polypropylene (PP) in the guts of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of insect larvae, associated with the degradation of polypropylene (PP) plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a genus of bacteria found in the guts of superworm larvae, associated with polystyrene digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Kluyvera is a genus of nitrogen-fixing bacteria found in the gut of mealworms, contributing to nitrogen fixation.</data>
