    <node id="PLASTIC DEGRADATION">
      <data key="d0">BIODEGRADATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Plastic degradation is the process by which synthetic plastic materials, such as polyethylene (PE), polystyrene (PS), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and polyurethane, are broken down into smaller particles or simpler compounds. This process is facilitated by biological agents, including insect larvae such as mealworms (Tenebrio molitor), superworms, and yellow mealworms, as well as their gut microbiomes. These organisms, along with bacteria and fungi, play a crucial role in reducing environmental pollution by metabolizing and converting plastics into biomass or smaller molecules through processes like depolymerization and mineralization.

The efficiency of plastic degradation varies depending on the type of plastic, with some materials like PS and PE being more readily broken down than others. Elevated metabolites such as trans-trans-muconic acid and 4-aminobenzoic acid in insect guts suggest the breakdown of plastic polymers. Enzymatic activity and microbial processes further contribute to the degradation of plastics in the environment. Overall, plastic degradation represents a promising biological approach to mitigating plastic waste and its environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic degradation refers to the breakdown of plastics in the environment, often studied in the context of microplastic formation and biodegradation by organisms like mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic degradation refers to the breakdown of plastic materials, such as polystyrene, by microorganisms or chemical processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56425bd62513be46b9165bfd84f0dd0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c</data>
    </node>
