    <node id="PLASTIC CONSUMPTION RATES">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Plastic consumption rates by mealworms are measured to evaluate their ability to degrade different types of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic consumption rates refer to the amount of polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene (PE) consumed by superworms and yellow mealworms, which varied depending on the larvae species and diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic consumption rates refer to the amount of plastic (PU, EVA, and PP) consumed by yellow mealworms, which is consistent with larval weight changes and survival rates.</data>
