    <node id="ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE &amp; TECHNOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that published studies on the biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by mealworms and waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal where evidence of polyethylene biodegradation by bacterial strains from the guts of plastic-eating waxworms was published in 2014.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that publishes research on environmental issues, including studies on the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that publishes research on environmental issues, including studies on plastic biodegradation by organisms like mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that publishes research on environmental issues, including biodegradation of plastics by organisms like mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is the journal where Yang et al. (2015a, 2015b) published their research on the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that publishes research on the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms and other environmental topics.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Science &amp; Technology is a journal that publishes research on the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms and their gut microorganisms.</data>
