    </node>
    <node id="HIGH-IMPACT POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">High-impact polystyrene (HIPS) is a type of plastic that mealworms can ingest and degrade, though its consumption depends on its crystallinity.&lt;SEP&gt;High-impact polystyrene is a mixture of polystyrene and polybutadiene, which can be degraded by certain bacterial strains.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3</data>
