      <data key="d1">Differential Scanning Calorimetry (DSC) is a technique used to measure the crystallinity of polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Differential scanning calorimetry (DSC) is used to analyze thermal properties, such as melting point changes in HDPE during biodegradation.</data>
