    <node id="GALLERIA MELLONELLA HOLOGENOME">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The Galleria mellonella hologenome refers to the combined genetic material of the wax moth and its associated microbiota, which plays a role in biodegradation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Galleria mellonella hologenome refers to the combined genetic material of the wax moth caterpillar and its associated microbiota, which supports its ability to metabolize long-chain hydrocarbons like beeswax.&lt;SEP&gt;The Galleria mellonella hologenome supports microbiota-independent metabolism of long-chain hydrocarbon beeswax, highlighting its unique metabolic capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Galleria mellonella hologenome study explores the microbiota-independent metabolism of long-chain hydrocarbons like beeswax, providing insights into biodegradation processes.</data>
