    <node id="SUSTAINABLE APPROACH">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">A sustainable approach to waste management involves using organisms like Tenebrio molitor to biodegrade plastics, reducing environmental pollution.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">**Klebsiella oxytoca** is a Gram-negative bacterial species that has been extensively studied for its environmental and biodegradation capabilities. The strain **Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182** is particularly notable, as it contains the **alkB gene**, which is involved in hydrocarbon degradation. This strain, along with others such as **JCM 1665** and **NBRC 102593**, has been confirmed using PCR techniques. 

Klebsiella oxytoca has been isolated from the gut of **Tenebrio molitor** (mealworms), where it plays a significant role in the biodegradation of **polystyrene**, a type of plastic waste. Research indicates that this bacterium can utilize polystyrene as a carbon source, leading to a measurable weight loss of **12.97 ± 1.05% over 60 days**. The presence of the alkB gene in Klebsiella oxytoca further supports its potential in breaking down hydrocarbons, including polystyrene, within the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.

In addition to its role in polystyrene degradation, Klebsiella oxytoca is also studied for its broader environmental applications, particularly in the biodegradation of alkanes and other hydrocarbons. This makes it a promising candidate for addressing plastic pollution and other environmental challenges. Overall, Klebsiella oxytoca, especially the ATCC 13182 strain, is a versatile bacterium with significant potential in biodegradation and environmental remediation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALKB GENE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The AlkB gene is involved in the biodegradation of alkanes and is used in phylogenetic studies to understand the evolutionary relationships among bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkB gene encodes alkane-1-monooxygenase, an enzyme involved in the degradation of alkanes, and was targeted for detection in Klebsiella oxytoca strains.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkB gene encodes alkane-1-monooxygenase, an enzyme involved in the oxidation of alkanes and potentially in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkB gene is a genetic sequence involved in the degradation of hydrocarbons, and its presence in Klebsiella oxytoca ATCC 13182 was confirmed through PCR amplification and sequencing.&lt;SEP&gt;The alkB gene is responsible for encoding alkane hydroxylase, an enzyme involved in the degradation of hydrocarbons, including polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALKANE-1-MONOOXYGENASE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Alkane-1-monooxygenase is an enzyme encoded by the alkB gene, involved in the degradation of alkanes.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane-1-monooxygenase is an enzyme encoded by the alkB gene, involved in the oxidation of alkanes and potentially in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane-1-monooxygenase is an enzyme that may be responsible for the degradation of polystyrene by Klebsiella oxytoca strains in Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane-1-monooxygenase is an enzyme that may play a key role in the degradation of polystyrene by Klebsiella oxytoca.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane-1-monoxygenase is an enzyme with a higher abundance in PP-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-678bd592bfdda3f6dd8f2a6659de7fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SERRATIA MARCESCENS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Serratia marcescens is a bacterial species involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene emulsion in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a bacterial species previously reported to be involved in plastic biodegradation, isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a bacterial strain associated with hydrocarbon degradation and bioremediation, found in the gut microbiome of PS-degrading mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a gut microorganism found in Tenebrio molitor that contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a bacterial strain isolated from Tenebrio molitor, studied for its role in PS emulsion biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a gut microorganism linked to PS biodegradation in insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a bacterial strain identified in the study, potentially contributing to the degradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Serratia marcescens is a symbiotic bacterium isolated from mealworms that contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
    </node>
