    <node id="16S RIBOSOMAL RNA GENE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is a molecular marker used in PCR to identify and classify bacterial strains, such as Klebsiella oxytoca.&lt;SEP&gt;The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used as a molecular marker to identify and confirm bacterial species, such as Klebsiella oxytoca, isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used as a molecular marker to identify and confirm bacterial strains in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is used for molecular identification and phylogenetic analysis of bacterial strains, including Klebsiella oxytoca.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PCR">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify DNA sequences, in this case, for sequencing and analysis of microbial genes.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a molecular biology technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences, such as the 16S ribosomal RNA gene and the alkB gene in Klebsiella oxytoca strains.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a molecular technique used to amplify and detect specific DNA sequences, such as the alkB gene and 16S ribosomal RNA gene in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a technique used to amplify and analyze DNA from the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae to study their role in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase chain reaction (PCR) is a technique used to amplify DNA sequences, such as the 16SrRNA gene, for bacterial identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a molecular biology technique used to amplify DNA segments, such as the 16S rRNA gene, for microbial identification.&lt;SEP&gt;Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) is a molecular technique used in the study to identify and sequence bacteria isolated from the guts of Tenebrio molitor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0</data>
    </node>
