    <node id="PHYLOGENETIC ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to evaluate the evolutionary relationships among bacterial strains based on their 16S rRNA sequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to infer evolutionary relationships among bacteria, particularly those involved in polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study evolutionary relationships, in this case, to compare the alkB gene sequence with other bacterial species.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships among bacterial strains based on gene sequences, such as the AlkB gene.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships among organisms, such as the analysis of alkane 1-monooxygenase genes in Gordonia spp.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships between the alkB gene sequences of Klebsiella oxytoca and other bacterial species.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is used to study the evolutionary relationships among nifH gene sequences from the gut microbiota of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships among bacterial strains based on their 16S rRNA sequences.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d71b4e70d7c620ee64c709aaeae634a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa1d3c9710e10c5eb533d8d791c93e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51daa29515cc5a431055291627bcb199&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57f3782f3c1c49764c4b911c60b37fed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIQUID CARBON-FREE BASAL MEDIUM (LCFBM)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">LCFBM is a medium used for the enrichment of PS-degrading microorganisms and characterization of PS film degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;LCFBM is a medium used in the study to culture bacteria and assess their ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Liquid carbon-free basal medium is a nutrient solution used to culture microorganisms, ensuring that the sole carbon source is the target substance, such as polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PCR (POLYMERASE CHAIN REACTION)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">PCR is a molecular technique used in the study to confirm the identity of bacterial strains, such as Klebsiella oxytoca, by amplifying the 16S ribosomal RNA gene.&lt;SEP&gt;PCR is a technique used to amplify DNA sequences, including the cox1 gene, for genetic identification and analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62</data>
