    <node id="MICROPLASTICS POLLUTION">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microplastics pollution refers to the environmental issue caused by small plastic particles, including polystyrene, which can be addressed through biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics pollution refers to the widespread contamination of the environment by small plastic particles, posing significant ecological and health risks.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
    </node>
