    </node>
    <node id="WHEAT BRAN (WB)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Wheat bran (WB) is a common feed for commercially reared insect larvae, such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is a feed material used to rear Tenebrio molitor larvae before they are tested for plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is the outer layer of the wheat kernel, often used as a dietary supplement or in animal feed.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran is a dietary component used as a control feed for mealworms in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran is a normal feedstock for Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus larvae, providing essential nutrients and enhancing their consumption of polypropylene (PP) foam.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
