    <node id="PET MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d0">MICROPLASTIC</data>
      <data key="d1">PET microplastics are small particles of polyethylene terephthalate that are studied for their biodegradation in organisms like Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;PET microplastics are small particles of polyethylene terephthalate that are studied for their biodegradation in organisms like Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;PET microplastics are small plastic particles derived from polyethylene terephthalate, which are consumed and biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PET microplastics are small plastic particles derived from polyethylene terephthalate, commonly found in freshwater environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGAR">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Agar is a biological reagent used to create agar-PET gel, which serves as a feeding substrate for Tenebrio molitor larvae in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance used as a control diet in the study to compare the survival and digestion rates of Tenebrio molitor larvae when fed with PET-agar mixtures.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used as a solidifying agent in culture media.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used to solidify culture media for bacterial growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used as a solidifying agent in microbial growth media.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance used as a medium to mix with PP polymers for feeding mealworms in biodegradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used as a control diet in biodegradation experiments with mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used as a control diet in biodegradation experiments with mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is used as an adhesive in biodegradation studies to mix with polyethylene powders, allowing mealworms to ingest and degrade the microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance used in experiments to mix with polyethylene (PE) for feeding insect larvae during biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance used in experiments to mix with polyethylene microplastics for feeding T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae during biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Agar is a gelatinous substance derived from seaweed, used to solidify culture media for microbial growth.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HFIP">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">1,1,1,3,3-Hexafluorisopropyl solvent (HFIP) is a chemical reagent used in the preparation of PET microplastics for biodegradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) is a solvent used to extract and analyze residual PET polymers in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;1,1,1,3,3-Hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) is a solvent used to dissolve PET for analysis during biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;1,1,1,3,3-Hexafluoroisopropanol (HFIP) is a solvent used to dissolve PET for analysis during biodegradation studies.</data>
