    </node>
    <node id="WB">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">WB (wheat bran) is a nutrient-rich control diet used in the study to compare the growth and survival rates of Tenebrio molitor larvae against those fed PET microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;WB refers to wheat bran, a common diet for Tenebrio molitor larvae used as a control in the study to compare the effects of PET feeding on gut microbial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is a nutrient-rich food source that supports the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae, allowing them to complete their life cycle.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is a nutrient-rich food source that supports the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae, allowing them to complete their life cycle.&lt;SEP&gt;WB (wheat bran) is used as a control diet in biodegradation studies to compare the effects of polyethylene microplastics on mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is a traditional diet for mealworms, used as a control in studies to compare the effects of plastic diets on gut microbiome composition.</data>
