    </node>
    <node id="CENTRAL CARBON METABOLISM">
      <data key="d0">BIODEGRADATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Central Carbon Metabolism (CCM) refers to the suite of compounds within basic cellular pathways that are influenced by plastic exposure in insects, affecting their metabolic responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Central carbon metabolism (CCM) is a study focus to understand the metabolic changes in insect larvae exposed to different plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Central carbon metabolism refers to the metabolic pathways in insects that can be impacted by exposure to plastic feed substrates.</data>
