      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer studied for its biodegradability in environmental contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer studied for its biodegradation potential, often compared to polystyrene in degradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer used in various applications, studied for its biodegradation potential.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer used in various applications, studied for its biodegradation properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer that has been studied for its biodegradability alongside polystyrene and phenol formaldehyde.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a synthetic polymer used in various applications, and its biodegradation has been investigated in microbial studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Poly(methyl methacrylate) is a transparent thermoplastic often used as a lightweight or shatter-resistant alternative to glass, also studied for its biodegradability.</data>
