    <node id="POLYSTYRENE WASTES">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Polystyrene wastes are a significant environmental pollutant due to their persistence and resistance to degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene wastes are a type of plastic waste that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, with factors affecting biodegradation rates studied in research.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene wastes are a type of plastic waste that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms and their gut microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene wastes are a significant environmental pollutant that can be biodegraded by organisms like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene wastes are a type of plastic waste that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, offering a potential solution for plastic pollution.</data>
