    <node id="H2O">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">H2O (water) is a byproduct of the biodegradation process of polyethylene by lesser waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;H2O (water) was added to the diet of mealworms to improve the biodegradation of polystyrene monomer and oligomer residues.&lt;SEP&gt;Water (H2O) plays a crucial role in supporting the growth of bacteria and microbiota, as well as providing oxygen for aerobic and anaerobic degradation of styrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Water (H2O) is included in Diet 2 to study its effect on the biodegradation of polystyrene and the formation of oligomers.&lt;SEP&gt;Water (H2O) plays a crucial role in enhancing polystyrene biodegradation by mealworms, improving their growth, survival rates, and gut microbial activity.</data>
