      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen content in the biomass and frass of mealworms varies depending on the diet, with implications for the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is a key element involved in the biochemical changes observed in the digestive system of mealworms, indicating intensive digestive processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen levels in mealworm frass decrease during polystyrene biodegradation, suggesting higher nitrogen retention due to oxidative stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen is a key nutrient that symbiotic bacteria help insects assimilate, particularly in nitrogen-deficient environments.</data>
