    <node id="LACTOCOCCUS LACTIS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactococcus lactis is a bacterial species identified in the study, potentially involved in the gut microbiome's metabolic activities and the degradation of environmental pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactococcus lactis is a bacterium from the Streptococcaceae family, found to be more abundant in the gut of mealworms fed with PS, suggesting a potential role in PS biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactococcus lactis is a bacterium identified in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, potentially involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactococcus lactis is a species of bacteria in the gut microbiome of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of plastics.</data>
