    <node id="LACTOBACILLUS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Lactobacillus bacteria are present in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae and are negatively correlated with PE-oxo and PE-reg diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria in the gut microbiome of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a genus of gut microbes found in mealworms and superworms, contributing to plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria significantly associated with the gut microbiome of mealworms when fed a diet containing LDPE and bran.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a genus of lactic acid bacteria found in the mealworm gut microbiome, significantly associated with the PE + bran diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is significantly associated with the PE + bran diet in mealworms, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation and gut microbiome adjustment.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of mealworms, contributing to their gut microbiome and digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactobacillus is a bacterial genus found in the gut microbiome of insect larvae, potentially involved in the biodegradation of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CLOSTRIDIUM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Clostridium bacteria are present in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae and are negatively correlated with the PS diet and nitrogen metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a bacterial genus identified in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly in Diet 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of anaerobic bacteria that can be stimulated by high nutrient diets and is involved in the production of short-chain fatty acids (SCFAs) in the gut.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria in the gut microbiome of mealworms, potentially involved in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the gut microbiomes of Tenebrio species, contributing to the biodegradation of polyethylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the mealworm gut microbiome, showing significant differences in abundance between feeding groups.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of mealworms, contributing to their gut microbiome and digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a genus of bacteria, some species of which are known to be nitrogen-fixing and have been isolated from the guts of nitrogen-fixing insects.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
