      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworm exuviae are the shed exoskeletons of mealworms, which can be used as a prebiotic material for gut microbiota.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIFE CYCLE">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The life cycle of Tenebrio molitor includes egg, larva, pupa, and beetle stages, and is studied to understand their ability to complete development while feeding on polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of Tenebrio molitor is studied to understand the effects of polystyrene consumption on larval development and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of Tenebrio molitor, from larvae to pupae and beetles, was monitored to assess the impact of polystyrene consumption on their development.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of mealworms is studied to understand their ability to complete development while feeding on plastics like polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of organisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, is studied to understand their ability to complete development while feeding on polystyrene wastes.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of yellow mealworms is studied to determine their ability to develop and reproduce even when fed polystyrene, indicating their resilience and potential for plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of larvae, including stages such as egg, larva, pupa, and adult, was considered in the study to understand the impact of plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of superworms and yellow mealworms includes egg, larva, pupa, and adult stages, with pupation rates being an indicator of their health and development.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of lesser waxworms is studied to understand their growth and development when fed polyethylene (PE) compared to their conventional food, waxcomb.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of the lesser waxworm includes stages such as larvae, pupae, moth, and egg, which were studied to assess its ability to complete development while feeding on polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of mealworms is studied to understand their ability to complete development when fed on polystyrene and other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The life cycle of Tenebrio molitor larvae is studied to understand the effects of different feed types on their development, mortality, and nutritional value.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
