      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Environmental impact refers to the effects of plastic waste on ecosystems, including marine and terrestrial environments, and the role of mealworms in mitigating this impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental impact refers to the effects of pollutants, such as microplastics, on ecosystems and organisms, often studied through toxicological assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental impact refers to the effects of substances like plastics and microplastics on ecosystems and organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd</data>
    </node>
