    <node id="BIODEGRADABLE PLASTICS">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Biodegradable plastics are designed to break down more easily in the environment, reducing pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials designed to break down more easily in the environment, often studied for their degradation by microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials that can be broken down by living organisms, such as mealworms, reducing their environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials that can be broken down by microorganisms, reducing environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials designed to break down more easily in the environment, potentially reducing plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials that can be broken down by organisms like mealworms, offering a potential solution to plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials that can be broken down by organisms like mealworms, offering a potential solution to plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradable plastics are materials designed to break down more easily in the environment, often through the action of microorganisms, reducing their environmental impact.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLASTIC POLLUTION">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plastic pollution is a significant environmental threat caused by the accumulation of non-biodegradable plastics in landfills and natural ecosystems, posing risks to human and environmental health.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, particularly petroleum-based plastics like polystyrene, which are resistant to natural degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, posing risks to ecosystems and organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, posing significant threats to ecosystems and wildlife.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, leading to ecological and human health concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, which can be addressed through biodegradation by organisms like mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, leading to ecological and health risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste, including polystyrene, in the environment, posing threats to ecosystems and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, particularly in marine ecosystems, causing harm to biodiversity.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, which poses significant threats to ecosystems, wildlife, and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic pollution refers to the accumulation of plastic waste in the environment, which can fragment into microplastics and cause adverse effects on ecosystems and human health.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MICROPLASTIC POLLUTION">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Microplastic pollution is a major environmental issue caused by the accumulation of plastic waste, which is challenging to degrade and harmful to ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastic pollution refers to the presence of small plastic particles in the environment, often found in water, soil, and organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastic pollution refers to the widespread contamination of environments by small plastic particles, affecting ecosystems and organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastic pollution refers to the widespread contamination of environments, including deep-sea sediments, by small plastic particles.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastic pollution refers to the environmental issue caused by the accumulation of small plastic particles, which can be addressed through the biodegradation capabilities of Tenebrio larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastic pollution refers to the widespread presence of small plastic particles in the environment, which pose significant threats to ecosystems, wildlife, and human health.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ENVIRONMENTAL SUSTAINABILITY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Environmental sustainability refers to practices and research aimed at reducing environmental impact and promoting sustainable resource use.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental sustainability research focuses on developing solutions to reduce the impact of pollutants, such as plastics, on ecosystems and human health.</data>
