    <node id="PU">
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
      <data key="d1">Epigenetic modification refers to changes in gene expression caused by polyurethane (PU) as a sole source of feed for mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyurethane (PU) is a type of plastic that can be degraded by gut bacteria in insects like yellow mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic that yellow mealworms can consume, leading to changes in their gut bacterial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;PU (Polyurethane) is a versatile polymer used in foams, coatings, adhesives, and elastomers, known for its durability and flexibility.</data>
