      <data key="d1">Tetradecanoic acid is a fatty acid detected in the chloroform extracts of frass, indicating enzymatic activity during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetradecanoic acid, also known as myristic acid, is a saturated fatty acid that is excreted by mealworms during the metabolism of PS-containing diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLEAMIDE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Oleamide is an amide detected in the chloroform extracts of frass, indicating enzymatic activity during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Oleamide is an amide that is excreted by mealworms during the metabolism of PS-containing diets, indicating enzymatic activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950</data>
