      <data key="d1">Tetradecanamide is an amide detected in the chloroform extracts of frass, indicating enzymatic activity during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetradecanamide is an amide that is excreted by mealworms during the metabolism of PS-containing diets, indicating enzymatic activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HEXADECANAMIDE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">A chemical compound identified in the gut intestine content of Tenebrio molitor larvae during polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexadecanamide is an amide detected in the chloroform extracts of frass, indicating enzymatic activity during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexadecanamide is an amide that is excreted by mealworms during the metabolism of PS-containing diets, indicating enzymatic activity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f141d484320c21ec01b892a9b7d56486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHOLESTEROL">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Cholesterol is a bioactive compound identified in the biomass of mealworms after the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS), indicating its role in the metabolic pathways involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Cholesterol is a metabolite detected in the chloroform extracts of frass, indicating enzymatic activity during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Cholesterol is a sterol that is excreted by mealworms and is indicative of enzymatic activity during the metabolism of PS-containing diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57edc76f6646a41c4845d94baa519950</data>
    </node>
