      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Inositol is a sugar alcohol found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly associated with plastic-based diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Inositol is a sugar alcohol whose utilization by larvae varies depending on the diet and plastic exposure.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DECANOIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Decanoic acid is a compound taken up by the gut microbiota of mealworms in the PE-oxo diet group.&lt;SEP&gt;Decanoic acid is a fatty acid whose utilization by larvae varies depending on the diet and plastic exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Decanoic acid is a saturated fatty acid found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly associated with polyethylene-based diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Decanoic acid levels in Tenebrio molitor larvae are negatively correlated with the first ordination axis in PCA analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADIPIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Adipic acid is a chemical compound whose utilization by larvae varies depending on the diet and plastic exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipic acid is a dicarboxylic acid found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly associated with cellulose-based diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Adipic acid levels in Tenebrio molitor larvae are positively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the first ordination axis in PCA analysis.</data>
