    </node>
    <node id="D-MELIBIOSE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">D-melibiose is a disaccharide found in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly associated with polyethylene-based diets.&lt;SEP&gt;D-melibiose is a sugar whose utilization by larvae varies depending on the diet and plastic exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;D-melibiose levels in Tenebrio molitor larvae are negatively correlated with the first ordination axis in PCA analysis.</data>
