      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Low-density polyethylene beads are used as bedding in habitats to study their interaction with mealworms and beetles.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEMON JUICE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Lemon juice (Realemon) is used as a pre-treatment for EPS cups to study its effect on mealworm consumption rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Lemon juice (Realemon) is used as a pre-treatment for EPS cups to study its effect on mealworm consumption rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Lemon juice is a pre-treatment used to enhance EPS consumption by mealworms in experimental studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Lemon juice is an acidic pre-treatment used to weaken the outer layer of EPS cups, increasing the consumption rate by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Lemon juice is a pre-treatment used to enhance EPS consumption by mealworms in experimental studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Lemon juice is an acidic pre-treatment used to weaken the outer layer of EPS cups, increasing the consumption rate by mealworms.</data>
