    <node id="COVID-19">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">COVID-19 is a global pandemic that has led to increased use of disposable face masks, contributing to environmental pollution from microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;COVID-19 is a global pandemic that led to a significant increase in the production and usage of disposable surgical masks, contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;COVID-19 is a viral disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 virus, which has been declared as no longer a global health emergency by the WHO in 2023.&lt;SEP&gt;COVID-19 restrictions led to variable experimental conditions, affecting mealworm behavior and EPS consumption rates.</data>
