    <node id="HEXATRIACONTANE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Hexatriacontane (C36H74) is a long-chain alkane found in the frass of aged PE-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating biodegradation of polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexatriacontane (C36H74) is a long-chain alkane found in the frass of aged PE-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating the breakdown of polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Hexatriacontane is a chemical compound used in the wax industry with the formula C36H74.</data>
