    <node id="MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE)">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworms are larvae of Tenebrio molitor that have been studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene and their gut microbiome responses to different diets.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PYRENE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Pyrene is a polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon (PAH) that can be degraded by Achromobacter denitrificans ASU-035.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LACCASE BIOCATALYSTS">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Laccase biocatalysts are enzymes identified from Pseudomonas species that are suitable for the degradation of synthetic textile dyes.</data>
