    </node>
    <node id="GUT MICROBIAL FLORA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Gut microbial flora refers to the community of microorganisms residing in the digestive tracts of organisms, which can play a role in biodegradation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial flora of certain organisms, such as mealworms, plays a significant role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DI-(2-ETHYLHEXYL) PHTHALATE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Di-(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate is a plasticizer commonly found in plastics and is the target of biodegradation by Achromobacter sp. RX.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROMOCRESOLGREEN DYE">
