    <node id="BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterial species involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium capable of deteriorating irradiation/high-temperature pretreated linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE).&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene, offering potential solutions for plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterium studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus amyloliquefaciens is a bacterial strain studied for its potential to biodegrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE).</data>
