    </node>
    <node id="DRIED WHEY">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Dried whey is a byproduct of cheese production, used as a feed ingredient, and analyzed here for its fatty acid composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is a feed component tested for Tenebrio molitor larvae, showing lower larval mortality but slower development rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is a feed supplement used in rearing Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to their nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is a feed used in experiments to study its impact on the life cycle and mortality of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is a feed used in the study to assess its effects on the crude protein and fat content of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is a protein-rich feed component used in the experiment, representing the protein diet group.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is another feed component used in the study, and its fatty acid content is compared to other feeds like wheat bran and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is another feed tested in the experiment, showing moderate mortality rates and occasional cannibalism among mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RAW WARE POTATOES">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Raw ware potatoes are a carbohydrate-rich feed component used in the experiment, representing the carbohydrate diet group.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw ware potatoes are a feed component tested for Tenebrio molitor larvae, resulting in lower larval mortality but slower development rates.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEED COMPOSITION">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Feed composition is a key factor influencing the development, mortality, and nutritional value of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEED">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Feed refers to the different dietary components (wheat bran, dried whey, and polystyrene) used to rear larvae in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Feed refers to the nutritional components provided to Tenebrio molitor larvae, influencing their development, mortality, and nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Feed refers to the nutritional components provided to Tenebrio molitor larvae, which can include wheat bran, potatoes, whey, and polystyrene, affecting their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LARVAL MORTALITY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Larval mortality is a key metric in the study of Tenebrio molitor, influenced by feed composition and environmental conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NITROGENOUS SUBSTANCES">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogenous substances are analyzed in Tenebrio molitor larvae to assess the nutritional impact of different feed types.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogenous substances are compounds analyzed in mealworms, reflecting their nutritional content and the impact of different feeds.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogenous substances are compounds found in Tenebrio molitor larvae and their excrement, increasing during polystyrene biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUSTAINABILITY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">Sustainability refers to the environmental and economic benefits of using Tenebrio molitor as an alternative protein source and for waste management.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREENHOUSE GAS EMISSIONS">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Greenhouse gas emissions are reduced through insect farming, making Tenebrio molitor a sustainable protein source.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARABLE LAND">
      <data key="d0">ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT</data>
      <data key="d1">Arable land use is minimized in insect farming, contributing to the sustainability of Tenebrio molitor production.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORIZON EUROPE">
