    <node id="SOXHLET EXTRACTION">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The Soxhlet extraction method is used to determine the fat content in samples, though the details of its application in this experiment are not fully described.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SELENIUM">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Selenium is used in the mineralization process of the Kjeldahl method to aid in the breakdown of organic material for nitrogen determination.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SULFURIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Sulfuric acid (H2SO4) is used in the mineralization process of the Kjeldahl method to break down organic material for nitrogen determination.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SODIUM HYDROXIDE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Sodium hydroxide (NaOH) is used in the distillation phase of the Kjeldahl method to neutralize acids and release ammonia for nitrogen determination.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BORIC ACID">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Boric acid (H3BO3) is used in the distillation phase of the Kjeldahl method to capture ammonia for nitrogen determination.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TASHIRO INDICATOR">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Tashiro indicator is used in the titration phase of the Kjeldahl method to determine the endpoint of the reaction for nitrogen content calculation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIFE CYCLE STUDY">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">A study conducted to analyze the life cycle and mortality of mealworms when fed different types of feed, including polystyrene foam.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="N-HEPTANE">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">N-heptane (CAS 142-82-5) is a chemical solvent used in the Soxhlet extraction method for determining fat content in samples.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOXHLET METHOD">
      <data key="d0">RESEARCH STUDY</data>
      <data key="d1">The Soxhlet method is a laboratory technique used for extracting fat content from samples using solvents like n-heptane.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FATTY ACID METHYL ESTERS (FAMES)">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Fatty acid methyl esters are compounds derived from lipids, analyzed using gas chromatography to determine the fatty acid profile of samples.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNDECANOIC ACID METHYL ESTER">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Undecanoic acid methyl ester is used as an internal standard in gas chromatography for the quantitative evaluation of fatty acid methyl esters.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAME MIXTURE C4-C24">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">FAME Mixture C4-C24 is a standard containing 37 selected fatty acids, used for external normalization in gas chromatography analysis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROWN–FORSYTHE TEST">
