    </node>
    <node id="POTATOES">
      <data key="d0">CHEMICAL</data>
      <data key="d1">Potatoes are a starchy vegetable used as a feed ingredient, and their fatty acid composition is compared with other feeds in this study.&lt;SEP&gt;Potatoes are used as a feed for Tenebrio molitor larvae, affecting their fatty acid content and growth rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Potatoes are used as feed for mealworm larvae, influencing their fatty acid profile, with a notable content of saturated and monoenoic fatty acids.&lt;SEP&gt;Potatoes were used as a feed in the experiment, resulting in the lowest mortality rates and no cannibalism among mealworms.</data>
