    </node>
    <node id="ENTEROBACTER SOLI">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Enterobacter soli is a bacterial strain isolated from mealworms, potentially involved in the degradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KLEBSIELLA GRIMMONTII">
      <data key="d0">ORGANISM</data>
      <data key="d1">Klebsiella grimmontii is a bacterial strain identified in the study, showing sensitivity to salt and potential involvement in polystyrene degradation.</data>
