    <edge source="YELLOW MEALWORMS" target="BIODEGRADATION">
      <data key="d3">163.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Yellow mealworms and their gut microbiome play a crucial role in the biodegradation of various plastics, including PP, PU, and EVA.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are involved in the biodegradation of plastics, including polyvinyl chloride (PVC) and polylactic acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a key role in the biodegradation of polyether-PU foam, breaking it down into simpler compounds&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a role in the biodegradation of polyether-PU foam, breaking it down into smaller fragments.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics such as PVC, LDPE, and Styrofoam through their gut microbial activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are studied for their ability to biodegrade various plastics, including polyether-polyurethane foam, polystyrene, and polyvinyl chloride.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics like PS and PU through their gut microbiome and feeding activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyurethane (PU) through oxidation and depolymerization processes in their guts.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene and polyurethane foams through consumption and digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of polypropylene materials, such as surgical masks, through their digestive processes and gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics and masks through their gut fungi and microbial community.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are known for their ability to biodegrade plastics, serving as a comparative reference for the biodegradation capabilities of Achroia grisea.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS), breaking it down into lower molecular weight substances.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are studied for their potential to biodegrade plastic materials such as PP, PU, and EVA through their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics through changes in their gut bacterial communities.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastic polymers, such as PP, PU, and EVA, through their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics, such as polyethylene and polypropylene, through microbial activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms play a key role in the biodegradation of plastics, breaking them down into smaller components.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868</data>
    </edge>
