    <edge source="YELLOW MEALWORMS" target="POLYURETHANE (PU)">
      <data key="d3">46.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Yellow mealworms are tested for their ability to degrade polyurethane (PU) wastes, particularly polyether-PU foam.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can biodegrade polyurethane (PU) foam, with consumption rates similar to those of superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms show a similar ingestion preference for polyurethane (PU) foam and degrade it through oxidation and depolymerization processes in their guts.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms were fed polyurethane (PU), showing significantly lower survival rates compared to superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms consume and degrade polyurethane (PU), leading to depolymerization and oxidation of the plastic&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of polyurethane (PU) through the activity of their gut microbiome.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </edge>
