    <edge source="YELLOW MEALWORMS" target="POLYPROPYLENE">
      <data key="d3">60.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Yellow mealworms are capable of degrading polypropylene plastics, such as those found in surgical masks, through their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can biodegrade polypropylene through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization, reducing plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can biodegrade polypropylene through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can ingest and degrade polypropylene materials, such as disposable surgical masks, through their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms ingest and partially degrade polypropylene from mask layers, contributing to the biodegradation of this plastic material.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can biodegrade polypropylene through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization, reducing plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760</data>
    </edge>
