    <edge source="YELLOW MEALWORMS" target="POLYPROPYLENE (PP)">
      <data key="d3">45.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Yellow mealworms can biodegrade polypropylene (PP), as reported in studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms have been confirmed to degrade polypropylene, contributing to plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can degrade polypropylene, though it is more difficult to degrade in masks compared to foam plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms consume and partially degrade polypropylene (PP), with changes in molecular weight and thermal stability observed&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) through the activity of their gut microbiome.</data>
