    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="ILLUMINA MISEQ">
      <data key="d3">35.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Illumina MiSeq is used to analyze the bacterial and fungal microbiome diversities in the guts of superworms and mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Illumina MiSeq platform was used to sequence and analyze the gut microbiome of larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is used to analyze the changes in gut bacterial and fungal microbiomes of yellow mealworms during the biodegradation of surgical masks.&lt;SEP&gt;Illumina MiSeq is used to study changes in gut bacterial and fungal diversities in yellow mealworms fed with surgical masks.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="ZOPHOBAS ARATUS">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Zophobas aratus is involved in the biodegradation of plastics, with changes in microbial communities observed during the process.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus is associated with its ability to biodegrade different types of plastics, including polypropylene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="PET">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae produces enzymes that break down PET into intermediate metabolites, facilitating its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of larvae is involved in the enzymatic breakdown and depolymerization of PET, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of larvae is involved in the enzymatic breakdown and depolymerization of PET, contributing to its biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="PET-FED GROUP">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The PET-fed group shows significant shifts in gut microbial communities compared to WB-fed and unfed groups, indicating the impact of PET on gut bacteria.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </edge>
