      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="TENEBRIO MONITOR">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Tenebrio monitor larvae changes during the biodegradation of cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="RESPIRATION ENHANCEMENT FACTORS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor secretes respiration enhancement factors that improve the degradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="MEALWORM">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of mealworms plays an essential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="GENTAMICIN SULFATE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gentamicin sulfate is used to suppress the gut microbiome of mealworms, allowing researchers to isolate the mealworm's role in plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="SUPERNATANT">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Supernatant contains secreted factors from the mealworm and its gut bacteria, which are analyzed to understand their role in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The supernatant derived from the gut microbiome contains factors that enhance the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="FALCON">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Falcon nylon cell strainers are used to filter gut bacteria samples during the collection process.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="POLYSTYRENE (PS)">
      <data key="d3">44.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Tenebrio larvae, including specific bacterial families, is essential for the depolymerization and chemical modification of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of insects plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) through enzymatic activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of mealworms contains bacteria that are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of mealworms is essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules and CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of mealworms secretes factors that enhance the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cc75b7e672a7f7c036713dfa2675d79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="ANTIBIOTICS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Antibiotics inhibit the gut bacteria of mealworms, reducing their ability to degrade polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOME" target="CARBON-FREE MEDIA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Carbon-free media is used to culture the gut microbiome of mealworms without introducing external carbon sources, ensuring accurate measurement of polystyrene degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6</data>
