    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="GUT MICROBIAL COMMUNITY">
      <data key="d3">36.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbial community of Tenebrio molitor larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polypropylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial community of mealworms plays a key role in the biodegradation of polyether-PU foam by breaking down the material.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial community of Tenebrio species plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polyethylene polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbial community of insect larvae plays a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="FRASS">
      <data key="d3">148.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation of EPS by Tenebrio molitor larvae results in the production of frass, a safe and reusable byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains degraded microplastics, providing evidence of the biodegradation process in mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains evidence of plastic biodegradation, including partially degraded plastics and new biodegraded products.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is the residual material excreted by mealworms after consuming polyether-PU, providing evidence of biodegradation and depolymerization&lt;SEP&gt;Frass, the excrement of mealworms, is analyzed to determine the extent of polystyrene degradation by the larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass from yellow mealworms contains residual mask materials and new organic substances, indicating the occurrence of biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains residual polymers and byproducts of biodegradation, providing insights into the degradation process&lt;SEP&gt;Frass analysis provides insights into the extent of polystyrene degradation by mealworms, showing changes in molecular weight and degradation products.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is analyzed to study the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is analyzed to study the degradation of polystyrene (PS) into lower molecular weight substances by larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains biodegraded polypropylene (PP) residues and intermediate compounds, indicating the degradation process by T. molitor and Z. atratus.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is analyzed to determine the extent of polypropylene foam biodegradation by larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains the biodegradation products of PE and PS microplastics, indicating the effectiveness of Tenebrio molitor larvae in breaking down these pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is analyzed to study the molecular weight changes and biodegradation of LDPE by mealworm larvae&lt;SEP&gt;Frass is analyzed to determine the extent of plastic biodegradation by yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass was analyzed to confirm the biodegradation of microplastics by mealworms&lt;SEP&gt;Frass provides insights into the biodegradation process of polystyrene by mealworms, containing degraded polymers and metabolic byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass, the excrement of mealworms, contains residual polystyrene and byproducts of biodegradation, indicating the extent of plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
