    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="DEPOLYMERIZATION">
      <data key="d3">69.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation involves the depolymerization of long-chain polymers into smaller molecules, as seen in the degradation of microplastics by larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is a critical step in the biodegradation of PET by mealworms, breaking down the polymer into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is a critical step in the biodegradation of PET by mealworms, breaking down the polymer into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is a key process in biodegradation, where long polymer chains are broken down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is a key process in the biodegradation of polyethylene by mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is a key step in the biodegradation of plastics, breaking down polymer chains into smaller units.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is the first step in the biodegradation process, where large polymer chains are broken down&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is the first essential step in the biodegradation of plastics, involving the breakdown of polymer chains.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7</data>
    </edge>
