      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Molecular weight reduction is a key indicator of plastic biodegradation, observed in the breakdown of polyethylene by bacterial strains.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight reduction occurs during the biodegradation of polyethylene by mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight reduction is a key measure of the biodegradation process, indicating the breakdown of polyethylene</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7</data>
    </edge>
