    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="POLYETHYLENE">
      <data key="d3">177.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation is a key process in breaking down polyethylene, reducing its environmental impact&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation is a key process in the breakdown of polyethylene by insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is biodegraded by yellow mealworms and dark mealworms, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is biodegraded by organisms such as Galleria mellonella and Enterobacter sp. D1.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation is the process by which polyethylene is broken down by insect larvae and their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation of polyethylene by larvae is incomplete and results in the generation of microplastics, limiting its effectiveness as a waste management strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is another plastic that has been studied for biodegradation by organisms like mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is a target of biodegradation processes, particularly by microbial consortia.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation is the process by which polyethylene is broken down by organisms like mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation is a process by which organisms like mealworms, superworms, and fungi break down polyethylene into simpler compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation processes, facilitated by organisms like Galleria mellonella and Tenebrio molitor, contribute to the breakdown of polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is a focus of biodegradation studies due to its widespread use and environmental persistence.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation of polyethylene (PE) by mealworms results in the conversion of ingested PE into CO2 and lower molecular weight compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is studied for its biodegradation by organisms such as caterpillars, addressing environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is biodegraded by mealworms, with the gut microbiome playing a significant role in the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is biodegraded by lesser waxworms, with the process enhanced by additional nutrition.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is degraded by the lesser waxworm, resulting in weight loss and the formation of holes in the PE film.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is the primary polymer studied for biodegradation by mealworms, with different types (LDPE, LLDPE, HDPE) showing varying degradation rates&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene is a target of biodegradation studies, particularly by insect larvae like plastic-eating waxworms and their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation is the process by which polyethylene is broken down by organisms such as mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c308c400b412f39f4adb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41af774fc28352c7dd95d8c3cb43f855</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="ENZYMATIC PROFILE">
      <data key="d3">48.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The enzymatic profile of Tenebrio molitor is crucial for the biodegradation of plastics like PVC and PLA.&lt;SEP&gt;The enzymatic profile of mealworms, including enzymes like esterases and β-glucosidase, is essential for the degradation of plastics and cellulose.&lt;SEP&gt;The enzymatic profile of organisms like Tenebrio molitor is crucial for the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The enzymatic profile of organisms like Tenebrio molitor changes during the biodegradation of cellulose, polyethylene, and polystyrene waste.&lt;SEP&gt;The enzymatic profile of insect larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The enzymatic profile of mealworms, including enzymes like esterases and β-glucosidase, is essential for the degradation of plastics and cellulose.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-767a2e5a2bde762f9c1b3dbbf7746d09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a603837ad5b989bafd614f5eeb8504c1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="GUT BACTERIA">
      <data key="d3">129.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut bacteria are crucial for the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor larvae and adults play a potential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor larvae play a key role in breaking down polyethylene (PE) into smaller, degradable components.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of plastics, such as polystyrene, by breaking down complex polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, as their suppression by gentamicin inhibits the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria isolated from mealworms are involved in the biodegradation of plastics, demonstrating their role in breaking down plastic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria play a crucial role in the biodegradation of synthetic and natural polymers by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by breaking down its polymer chains.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of EPS, aiding in the breakdown of the plastic material&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in insects like Tenebrio molitor play a key role in the biodegradation of plastics by producing enzymes.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, facilitating its breakdown into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of LDPE, as their suppression by gentamicin reduces degradation efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms play a critical role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by facilitating enzymatic breakdown.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria play a crucial role in the biodegradation of synthetic and natural polymers by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, as demonstrated by the suppression of degradation when antibiotics like gentamicin are used.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1f3d7160b00e54118a03f0273d60bfe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </edge>
