    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="PLASTIC WASTE">
      <data key="d3">163.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation is a potential solution to reduce plastic waste by breaking it down into simpler compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation offers a potential solution to plastic waste by breaking down plastics into less harmful substances.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste can be biodegraded by organisms like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus, contributing to environmental remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is a focus of biodegradation studies, with organisms like mealworms and waxworms offering potential solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste can be biodegraded by organisms such as Tenebrio molitor, offering a sustainable solution to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including polystyrene, can be biodegraded by mealworms and their gut microbiome, offering a potential solution to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is a major environmental pollutant that is the focus of biodegradation research, particularly involving microorganisms and insects&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is the target of biodegradation processes, such as those carried out by the lesser wax-worm.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including polystyrene, is the target material for biodegradation by mealworms in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is the target of biodegradation efforts involving organisms like mealworms and wax moth caterpillars&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is a target for biodegradation research, with mealworms and their gut bacteria offering potential solutions for its degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including PET, is mitigated through the biodegradation capabilities of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including PET, is mitigated through the biodegradation capabilities of mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including PS and LDPE, is targeted for biodegradation by mealworms as a potential solution to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste, including polystyrene and polyethylene, can be biodegraded by mealworms, offering a potential solution for environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The biodegradation of plastics by Tenebrio larvae offers a potential solution to the global issue of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic waste is a major environmental issue, and biodegradation is a key solution for its management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463ac9dfa68274d35700c61208f4ea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="STURM-TEST">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Sturm-test is used to investigate the biodegradation of plastics in laboratory settings.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="GUT BACTERIAL-MICROBIOME">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut bacterial-microbiome of insect larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20</data>
