    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="EPS">
      <data key="d3">41.0</data>
      <data key="d4">EPS is a plastic that undergoes biodegradation by gut microorganisms in mealworms, as indicated by changes in microbial flora.&lt;SEP&gt;EPS undergoes biodegradation by mealworms, evidenced by molecular weight reduction and chemical changes&lt;SEP&gt;EPS is biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, reducing its environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Expanded polystyrene (EPS) undergoes biodegradation, with significant mass loss observed during experiments involving mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
