    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="SUPERWORMS">
      <data key="d3">96.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Superworms are being investigated for their potential to biodegrade Styrofoam through their gut system.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms are capable of degrading polyethylene (PE) and other plastics, contributing to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms play a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics, such as low-density polyethylene and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene through their gut microbiota and enzymatic activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms play a key role in the biodegradation of Styrofoam through their consumption and gut bacteria activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and polyurethane (PU) through oxidation and depolymerization processes in their guts.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms contribute to the biodegradation of plastics, aiding in the reduction of environmental plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene and polyurethane foams through consumption and digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms play a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics such as PS, PU, and LDPE, with higher consumption rates for PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms play a significant role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by breaking it down into lower molecular weight substances.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms contribute to the biodegradation of polypropylene, highlighting their potential in addressing plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c</data>
