    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA">
      <data key="d3">55.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Klebsiella oxytoca contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene by breaking it down in the gut of Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene through enzymatic activity.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene through the activity of the alkB gene.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca, found in mealworm guts, plays a key role in the biodegradation of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca, found in the gut of mealworms, plays a key role in the biodegradation of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor's gut and is potentially involved in polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca is hypothesized to contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene through the secretion of extracellular oxidative enzymes.</data>
