      <data key="d3">86.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut microorganisms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene by Alphitobius diaperinus.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, indicating their critical role in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are directly involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene, contributing to its breakdown.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of plastics, breaking down complex polymers into simpler compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms, such as Klebsiella oxytoca, play a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, contributing to the breakdown of plastic into simpler compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, breaking it down into simpler compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of plastics such as polystyrene, polyvinyl chloride, and polylactide.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microorganisms in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, highlighting their role in plastic degradation.</data>
