    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="MEALWORM">
      <data key="d3">35.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are a key model in plastic biodegradation studies, demonstrating their ability to break down plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of microplastics, offering a practical approach to managing plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of synthetic polymers like polystyrene and polyethylene, offering a potential solution to environmental pollution&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms play a role in the biodegradation of plastics, as evidenced by their metabolic changes and plastic weight loss post-exposure.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
