    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="FTIR ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">32.0</data>
      <data key="d4">FTIR analysis confirmed the biodegradation of polyethylene by detecting new chemical groups in the egested frass of Achroia grisea.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis detects changes in the chemical structure of polystyrene in frass, providing evidence of biodegradation and ring cleavage.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis is used to confirm the biodegradation and oxidation of EPS and LDPE in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;FTIR analysis is used to study the chemical changes in microplastics during biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
