      <data key="d4">Firmicutes dominates the gut microbiome of PS- and CS-fed larvae, suggesting its importance in the biodegradation of these materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmicutes in the gut microbiome of mealworms contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmicutes, a phylum in the gut microbiota of mealworms, shows significant changes in abundance during polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmicutes, a phylum of bacteria in the gut of mealworms, contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Firmicutes plays a role in the biodegradation of organic materials like polystyrene in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus.</data>
