    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="MICROBIOME">
      <data key="d3">36.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The microbiome in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae supports the biodegradation of styrene and its derivatives, leading to the formation of CO2 and H2O.&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome of insects plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, including polystyrene and polyolefins.&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome of insects plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, including polystyrene and polyolefins.&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome, particularly gut microbiota in insects, plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics like polystyrene.</data>
