      <data key="d4">Pseudomonas bacteria isolated from mealworms can degrade bioplastics, suggesting their involvement in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas exhibits significant differences in the gut microbiome of PS-fed larvae, indicating its involvement in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas is involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene, as evidenced by its abundance in polystyrene-fed samples.</data>
