    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTANT">
      <data key="d3">42.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation of polyethylene by mealworms offers a potential solution to reduce the environmental impact of plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation processes, such as those carried out by insect larvae, are essential for mitigating the impact of environmental pollutants like plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Biodegradation processes, such as those carried out by insect larvae, are essential for mitigating the impact of environmental pollutants like plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental pollutants like plastics are targeted for biodegradation to reduce pollution&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene and polyethylene, as environmental pollutants, are targeted for biodegradation by organisms like mealworms and waxworms.</data>
