    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">88.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enzymes are biological catalysts that play a key role in the degradation of synthetic plastics by breaking down complex polymer structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes are key components in the biodegradation process of polypropylene (PP) by Tenebrio molitor larvae and their gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes such as cholesterol esterases, proteases, and lipases are involved in the biodegradation of polyurethane by breaking its chemical bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes such as CYP6/4, Lac640, and SOD are involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene and lignocellulose by Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes play a critical role in the biodegradation of plastics by breaking down complex polymers into simpler, more manageable compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes play a critical role in the biodegradation of plastics by breaking down complex polymers into simpler, more manageable compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes secreted by the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae are essential for the biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Enzymes secreted by the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae facilitate the oxidation and depolymerization of aged PE and PS microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d</data>
    </edge>
