    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="MICROPLASTICS (MPS)">
      <data key="d3">24.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation by mealworms effectively breaks down microplastics (MPs) into smaller particles, reducing their environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics (MPs) are generated during the biodegradation process by macroinvertebrates such as Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics (MPs) are subject to biodegradation by mealworms, with the process influenced by the type of polyethylene and its properties.</data>
