    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="METABOLIC PATHWAYS">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodegradation of polystyrene and lignocellulose involves specific metabolic pathways, including oxidation, aromatic ring cleavage, and fatty acid metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic pathways are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) and lignocellulose (CS) by mealworms, involving enzymatic degradation and mineralization.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
