    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="T. MOLITOR">
      <data key="d3">40.0</data>
      <data key="d4">T. molitor contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene through the activity of its gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae play a significant role in the biodegradation of polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae contribute to the biodegradation of polystyrene foam, though to a lesser extent than T. obscurus.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor is essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae are involved in the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP), showing broad depolymerization patterns.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df</data>
    </edge>
