      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Changes in molecular weights of residual PS and LDPE confirm the depolymerization and biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight changes are analyzed to evaluate the degradation of polyethylene polymers by Tenebrio species, indicating the extent of biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight changes in polyethylene polymers indicate depolymerization during biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight changes are used to assess the efficiency of biodegradation of polyethylene microplastics by mealworms</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff</data>
    </edge>
