    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="MOLECULAR WEIGHT">
      <data key="d3">34.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lower molecular weight polymers are more easily biodegraded compared to higher molecular weight polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular weight plays a significant role in the biodegradation of polyethylene, with lower molecular weight polymers being more easily degraded.&lt;SEP&gt;The molecular weight of polyethylene (PE) affects its biodegradability, with lower molecular weight polymers being more easily degraded by insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;The molecular weight of polystyrene polymers influences the efficiency and pattern of biodegradation by mealworms.</data>
