      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS LARVAE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Zophobas atratus larvae are capable of biodegrading plastics, reducing plastic waste in the environment.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION" target="ULOMA SP.">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Uloma sp. can degrade plastics, playing a role in reducing plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Uloma sp. larvae are studied for their ability to degrade plastics, similar to mealworms.</data>
