    <edge source="DEPOLYMERIZATION" target="TENEBRIO MOLITOR">
      <data key="d3">130.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms contribute to the depolymerization of PVC, breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor contributes to the depolymerization of polyether-PU foam, breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor facilitates the depolymerization of plastics, breaking them down into smaller units.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the depolymerization of PET, breaking down long-chain polymers into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of depolymerizing plastic polymers like polystyrene and low-density polyethylene, a key step in biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae facilitate the depolymerization of polystyrene (PS) and low-density polyethylene (LDPE), with some processes being dependent on gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor contributes to the depolymerization of polyethylene, breaking down polymer chains into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of depolymerizing various plastics, including LLDPE, HDPE, and LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor facilitates the depolymerization of polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the depolymerization of polystyrene (PS), though less efficiently than Tenebrio obscurus.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is involved in the depolymerization of polypropylene (PP), breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae facilitate the depolymerization of polypropylene, breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae facilitate the depolymerization of polypropylene, breaking it down into smaller units.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the depolymerization of polyethylene (PE), a process that is not entirely dependent on gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae exhibit a broad depolymerization pattern during the biodegradation of LDPE, breaking down long-chain polymers into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae facilitate the depolymerization of LDPE, breaking it down into smaller molecules.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9</data>
    </edge>
