      <data key="d3">24.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Depolymerization is observed in the biodegradation of polystyrene, with the molecular weight of PS being reduced in the frass.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) undergoes depolymerization in the guts of superworms and yellow mealworms, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is the process by which polystyrene is broken down into smaller molecules by the gut microbes of insect larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997</data>
    </edge>
