    <edge source="DEPOLYMERIZATION" target="MEALWORMS">
      <data key="d3">40.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms facilitate the depolymerization of polystyrene (PS) by chewing and breaking down the polymer chains.&lt;SEP&gt;Older mealworms are capable of depolymerizing microplastics, breaking down long-chain polymers into smaller fragments&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms facilitate the depolymerization of polystyrene, leading to the formation of lower molecular weight fragments&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms facilitate the depolymerization of polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecular fragments.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
