    </edge>
    <edge source="DEPOLYMERIZATION" target="FRASS">
      <data key="d3">31.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Frass analysis reveals the depolymerization of microplastics by mealworms, particularly at the old larval stage&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains depolymerized residues of plastics like EPS and LDPE, indicating the biodegradation process by Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;Frass samples show evidence of depolymerization, with the breakdown of long-chain polymers into smaller units during plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains residual polymers, providing evidence of the depolymerization process in Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
