    <edge source="DEPOLYMERIZATION" target="POLYSTYRENE (PS)">
      <data key="d3">85.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Depolymerization is the process by which mealworms break down polystyrene polymers into smaller molecules, with efficiency varying based on polymer MW.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization is the process by which mealworms break down polystyrene polymers into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization occurs during the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms, breaking it into smaller molecular units.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization of PS occurs during biodegradation by mealworms, leading to reduced molecular weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Depolymerization of polystyrene occurs in the mealworm gut, leading to molecular weight changes&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) undergoes depolymerization in the guts of mealworms, resulting in lower molecular weight components.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene undergoes depolymerization in the guts of Tenebrio molitor larvae, leading to a decrease in molecular weight and the formation of smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) undergoes depolymerization in the guts of superworms and yellow mealworms, breaking down long-chain polymers into smaller units.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene undergoes depolymerization during the biodegradation process, breaking down into smaller molecular units.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="DEPOLYMERIZATION" target="GPC ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">24.0</data>
      <data key="d4">GPC analysis is used to characterize the depolymerization of plastics like PS and LDPE by Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis shows a decrease in the molecular weight of residual polystyrene in frass, indicating the extent of depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to study changes in molecular weight distribution, providing evidence of PP depolymerization by larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec</data>
    </edge>
