      <data key="d3">40.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LDPE undergoes depolymerization when consumed by Tenebrio molitor larvae, with different patterns observed compared to EPS&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE undergoes significant depolymerization in the digestive systems of mealworms, leading to a reduction in molecular weight.&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE undergoes depolymerization when digested by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae, reducing its molecular weight&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE undergoes depolymerization when ingested by mealworms, breaking down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Low-density polyethylene (LDPE) undergoes depolymerization by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae, even when gut bacteria are suppressed.</data>
