    <edge source="BRAN" target="MEALWORM LARVAE">
      <data key="d3">58.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bran is a primary component of the diet fed to mealworm larvae, used as a control and mixed with polystyrene in experimental diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a co-diet alongside polyethylene (PE) to feed mealworm larvae in biodegradation experiments&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation improves the biodegradation efficiency of polyethylene microplastics by mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation mitigates oxidative stress and improves the physiological performance of mealworm larvae during PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation reduces oxidative stress and improves the survival and biomass levels of mealworm larvae during PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Supplementing bran enhances the biomass and survival of mealworm larvae but slightly reduces their PE removal efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Supplementing bran in the diet of mealworm larvae mitigates oxidative stress and improves their survival and biomass levels during polyethylene biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="TENEBRIO MOLITOR">
      <data key="d3">115.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bran enhances the rate of polystyrene degradation by mealworms, with higher bran-to-PS ratios leading to increased consumption and survival rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is a dietary component fed to Tenebrio molitor larvae, influencing their gut microbiome and potentially their plastic degradation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is a dietary component used in experiments to study its impact on the gut microbiota and polystyrene biodegradation in Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a co-diet to enhance mealworm survival and reduce oxidative stress during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a dietary component in experiments to study its effect on the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a dietary component for mealworms to study its impact on the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a control diet for mealworms to compare the effects of microplastic consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a control diet to compare the effects of plastic consumption on Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a nutrient-rich food source for Tenebrio molitor larvae, supporting their growth and development when plastic foam is insufficient.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a control substrate in experiments involving Tenebrio molitor to compare its effects with plastic degradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a dietary supplement to support the survival and growth of mealworms during plastic biodegradation experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation improves the survival and PS degradation rates of mealworms, demonstrating the role of nutrition in enhancing biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran improves the consumption and biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by Tenebrio molitor larvae, supporting their survival and growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a codiet in feeding experiments with Tenebrio molitor to study its effect on polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a control food source to compare the survival and consumption rates of Tenebrio molitor larvae</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="OXIDATIVE STRESS">
      <data key="d3">30.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bran supplementation alleviates oxidative stress in Tenebrio molitor larvae during the biodegradation of microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation alleviates oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of PE microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran supplementation reduces oxidative stress in mealworm larvae by mitigating the effects of PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran, as a co-diet, reduces oxidative stress in plastic-degrading larvae by enhancing metabolic activities and antioxidant defenses.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="OXIDATIVE STRESS LEVELS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Oxidative stress levels in mealworm larvae are alleviated by supplementing bran during PE biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="BIOMASS LEVELS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biomass levels of mealworm larvae are enhanced by supplementing bran, improving their survival during PE biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="PE REMOVAL EFFICIENCY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PE removal efficiency is slightly reduced in mealworm larvae when bran is supplemented.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BRAN" target="MEALWORMS">
      <data key="d3">210.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bran is used as a control diet for mealworms to compare their survival and behavior with polystyrene-fed groups&lt;SEP&gt;Bran is used as a control diet for mealworms, showing lower nitrogen-fixing activity compared to Styrofoam-fed mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran plays a significant role in enhancing the survival, growth, and plastic degradation capabilities of mealworms. When co-fed with polystyrene (PS) or other plastics, bran improves the consumption and degradation rates of these materials by mealworms. Higher bran-to-PS ratios lead to increased plastic consumption and survival rates, as bran provides essential nutrients that support the mealworms' metabolism and growth, which are otherwise lacking in plastic-only diets. 

Bran is frequently used as a control or supplementary diet in experiments to study its influence on mealworm behavior, particularly their ability to degrade plastics like polystyrene and polyurethane (PU) foam. It has been observed that mealworms consume bran more efficiently than PU foam, as bran fulfills their nutritional needs. Additionally, bran supplementation not only enhances the mealworms' ability to degrade polystyrene but also supports their survival and growth over multiple generations. 

Furthermore, bran influences the mealworms' gut microbiome, which is crucial for their plastic biodegradation efficiency. It is used in various feeding experiments to compare the effects of microplastic consumption on mealworm growth, metabolism, and survival. Overall, bran serves as a vital dietary supplement that enables mealworms to thrive while effectively degrading plastic waste, making it a key component in studies focused on plastic biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bran was used as a control feed to compare the effects of microplastic ingestion on mealworms</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692</data>
    </edge>
