    <edge source="FRASS" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Frass contains degraded polystyrene and other compounds formed during the biodegradation process in insect larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains degraded polystyrene, indicating the role of mealworms in the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass contains residues of consumed polystyrene, indicating the degradation process by Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is broken down into various organic compounds found in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass from mealworms fed with polystyrene shows changes in nitrogen content and mineral composition, indicating the effects of biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is degraded and excreted as frass by insects, showing changes in molecular weight and thermal stability.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is excreted in the frass of insects, with the formation of PS-derived oligomers indicating biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Frass from larvae is analyzed to study the biodegradation of polystyrene, providing insights into the degradation process</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
