    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYLACTIC ACID (PLA)">
      <data key="d3">91.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can consume and degrade polylactic acid (PLA), a biodegradable plastic&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are used in a circular approach for managing PLA waste, involving resource recovery and fertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polylactic acid (PLA), offering a sustainable waste management solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae have been tested for the biodegradation of polylactic acid in laboratory settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PLA microplastics at a higher rate compared to PS and PVC, with minimal physiological stress when supplemented with bran.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade and assimilate polylactic acid (PLA) for energy supplementation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been found to biodegrade polylactic acid, aiding in the breakdown of this biodegradable plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been found to biodegrade polylactic acid, aiding in the breakdown of this biodegradable plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polylactic acid (PLA), offering a sustainable approach for waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading polylactic acid (PLA), a biodegradable plastic derived from renewable resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading polylactic acid (PLA), a biodegradable plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polylactic acid, a hydrolyzable bioplastic.</data>
