    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="NITROGEN FIXATION">
      <data key="d3">78.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are studied for their ability to fix nitrogen, which may be linked to their plastic-degrading capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation is studied in Tenebrio molitor to understand its metabolic capabilities during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor benefits from nitrogen fixation carried out by bacteria in its digestive tract, which supports its growth and development.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor exhibits nitrogen fixation capabilities, which are linked to its gut microbiome and plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae rely on nitrogen-fixing bacteria to supplement their nitrogen supply when fed a nitrogen-deficient diet of PP.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in the gut of Tenebrio molitor contribute to the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms utilize nitrogen fixation, facilitated by gut microbiota, to supplement nitrogen when consuming nitrogen-deficient plastic diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation is studied in plastic-eating mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) and their diazotrophic communities, which may play a role in their ability to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms utilize nitrogen-fixing bacteria in their digestive tract to assimilate atmospheric nitrogen, promoting their survival.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a81144d30653377d6d90e26c4497eb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edad11f4e8936fcfb69f8616ad364f18&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </edge>
