    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GUT MICROBIOTA">
      <data key="d3">362.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiota of *Tenebrio molitor*, commonly known as mealworms, plays a multifaceted and crucial role in both the biodegradation of synthetic polymers and the insect's overall metabolic processes. This microbiota is essential for breaking down a variety of plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polypropylene (PP), polyurethane (PU), and polyethylene microplastics. The microorganisms within the gut produce specific enzymes and metabolic pathways that facilitate the depolymerization and degradation of these materials, making *Tenebrio molitor* a promising candidate for applications in environmental science and waste management.

In addition to its role in plastic biodegradation, the gut microbiota is vital for the insect's digestion and adaptation to varying environmental conditions. Specific bacterial genera, such as *Mixta tenebrionis*, show increased abundance during the consumption of certain plastics like PVC, highlighting the dynamic interaction between the microbiota and the host. This adaptability underscores the microbiota's importance in supporting the insect's survival on plastic-based diets.

The gut microbiota's enzymatic activity and metabolic capabilities not only aid in plastic degradation but also contribute to nitrogen fixation, enabling mealworms to thrive on plastic diets. Studies have shown that the suppression of the gut microbiota by antibiotics inhibits the degradation of polystyrene, further confirming its essential role in plastic biodegradation.

Overall, the gut microbiota of *Tenebrio molitor* is a key component in the biodegradation of plastics, contributing to the breakdown of materials like polystyrene, PET, PVC, PP, PU, and polyethylene microplastics. Its dynamic interaction with the host and its ability to adapt to plastic-based diets highlight its potential for addressing plastic pollution and advancing environmental sustainability. The gut microbiota's role in the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) and polystyrene (PS) is particularly emphasized, as it influences the depolymerization process and supports the degradation of these materials. This makes the gut microbiota of *Tenebrio molitor* an essential player in the biodegradation of waste materials, including plastics, and a valuable resource for environmental sustainability efforts.</data>
      <data key="d5">10&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e540abd667582c77f4d2222836147ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68f3ddf96d927254424a036cd8b9acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491</data>
