    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d3">155.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) can chew and degrade Styrofoam, a type of expanded polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) can eat and degrade Styrofoam, contributing to the reduction of plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are capable of biodegrading Styrofoam, following a similar pattern of degradation as thermocol.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can consume and degrade Styrofoam, contributing to its biodegradation without adverse health effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade Styrofoam, contributing to the reduction of environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae consume Styrofoam, and their gut microbes play a crucial role in its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae have a proven ability to consume and degrade Styrofoam, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade Styrofoam, a form of expanded polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can efficiently degrade Styrofoam in their gut, converting it into CO2 and biomass.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can ingest and degrade Styrofoam, a form of polystyrene, into smaller fragments and eventually mineralize it into CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade Styrofoam through the action of their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can biodegrade Styrofoam, making them a potential solution for managing polystyrene waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can biodegrade styrofoam, with their gut bacteria playing a key role in the process, though it affects their growth and reproduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can biodegrade Styrofoam, contributing to the reduction of environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade Styrofoam, a form of expanded polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can biodegrade styrofoam, a common polystyrene product, through the action of their gut microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume and degrade Styrofoam, a form of polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam, a form of polystyrene, can influence the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae, potentially causing toxic effects.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027</data>
