    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="FOOD SAFETY">
      <data key="d3">60.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Food safety assessments are necessary when using Tenebrio molitor for biodegradation, as it may also serve as a food source.&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies evaluate the safety and nutritional value of mealworms as a potential food source for humans and livestock.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been assessed for food safety, confirming its suitability as a novel protein source.&lt;SEP&gt;Studies are being conducted to determine if Tenebrio molitor larvae that degrade Styrofoam are safe for human or animal consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Food safety considerations are relevant when studying Tenebrio molitor as an alternative protein source, especially when exposed to plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are being studied for their potential as a safe and sustainable alternative protein source.&lt;SEP&gt;The safety of Tenebrio molitor as a food source has been assessed, confirming its suitability for human and animal consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;The safety of mealworms as a food source is assessed by studying the impact of polystyrene consumption on their nutritional value and potential toxicity.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-372aa232f6e8aad1d8e0a93f16a42b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE">
      <data key="d3">149.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can ingest and partially degrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE), though the process is less efficient compared to other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene, contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene, with gut microbes playing a key role.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can also biodegrade low-density polyethylene, further aiding in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can depolymerize low-density polyethylene, but the process is less dependent on gut bacteria compared to polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene, indicating its potential in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade low-density polyethylene, highlighting their role in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene, contributing to environmental remediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE) with the help of their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade low-density polyethylene through both gut-microbe-dependent and independent depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae have been studied for their ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene (LDPE).&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene, further aiding in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can biodegrade low-density polyethylene, with varying degrees of depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene through gut-microbe-dependent processes.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee</data>
