    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">138.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are capable of consuming and degrading expanded polystyrene (EPS), contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can degrade expanded polystyrene (EPS), contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade expanded polystyrene through the action of its intestinal microbes, reducing environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading expanded polystyrene, offering a potential solution to environmental pollution caused by EPS waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, addressing environmental pollution issues.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae have been studied for their ability to biodegrade expanded polystyrene, offering a potential solution to plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, contributing to the reduction of environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, reducing its environmental impact.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, offering a potential solution to plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, as demonstrated in environmental studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is capable of chewing and degrading expanded polystyrene (EPS), contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade expanded polystyrene, contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bae14ee5ac26fe661b539bccaa825fb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b79a6f4c112b0b62ada6756140e3e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LINEAR LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms cannot ingest or degrade linear low-density polyethylene (LLDPE), likely due to its higher crystallinity.</data>
