      <data key="d3">34.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can biodegrade polypropylene (PP), contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can consume PP, though it provides minimal nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can depolymerize polypropylene (PP), but the process is nearly stopped under antibiotic suppression.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can depolymerize polypropylene (PP), but the process is nearly stopped under antibiotic suppression.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polypropylene (PP), demonstrating their ability to degrade various plastics.</data>
