    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KLEBSIELLA OXYTOCA">
      <data key="d3">55.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Klebsiella oxytoca is a bacterium isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, suggesting its potential role in polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca strains were isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, indicating their role in polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor harbors Klebsiella oxytoca in its gut, which plays a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut of Tenebrio molitor contains Klebsiella oxytoca strains that may contribute to the degradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca, isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, plays a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca is a gut bacterium of Tenebrio molitor involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene emulsion.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
