    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PET">
      <data key="d3">251.0</data>
      <data key="d4">**PET and Tenebrio molitor (Mealworms):**

Tenebrio molitor larvae, commonly known as mealworms, have been extensively studied for their remarkable ability to biodegrade polyethylene terephthalate (PET), a widely used plastic material. These larvae can break down PET through a combination of enzymatic, microbial, and metabolic processes. Their gut microbiota plays a crucial role in this biodegradation, as it shifts in response to PET feeding, facilitating the breakdown of the polymer. Additionally, the larvae's digestive enzymes contribute significantly to the process, enabling the depolymerization and molecular weight reduction of PET.

The efficiency of PET degradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae is influenced by factors such as the polymer's molecular weight and crystallinity degree. Studies have shown that the larvae can chew PET into smaller fragments, leading to significant mass reduction and depolymerization. Interestingly, some research suggests that Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PET independently of gut microbes, highlighting a unique capability compared to other plastics. This ability allows the larvae to use PET as an energy source, further contributing to the breakdown of this environmental pollutant.

Overall, Tenebrio molitor larvae demonstrate a promising potential for addressing plastic waste, particularly PET, through their natural biodegradation processes involving gut microbiota, digestive enzymes, and metabolic pathways. Their ability to degrade PET polymers efficiently makes them a subject of significant interest in environmental and waste management research.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8</data>
    </edge>
