      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae are commonly fed wheat bran (WB) in commercial rearing, which supports their growth and biodegradation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran (WB) is used as feed for Tenebrio molitor larvae before they are tested for plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran is used as a control diet for mealworms in biodegradation experiments, providing a baseline for comparison.&lt;SEP&gt;Wheat bran enhances the consumption of polypropylene (PP) foam by Tenebrio molitor larvae, providing essential nutrients.</data>
