    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STARVATION">
      <data key="d3">54.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms exhibit physiological responses to starvation, such as changes in energy distribution, when fed insufficient food like polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation in Tenebrio molitor larvae results in a decrease in reserve density and volumetric length, indicating insufficient energy for somatic maintenance.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation influenced the initial forced eating behavior of Tenebrio molitor larvae when fed PET-agar.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation is used as a control condition to assess the survival and weight changes of mealworms without food.&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation is a treatment condition used to evaluate the survival and PS consumption of Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;Starvation negatively impacts the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae, reducing their ability to reach the pupation stage.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb</data>
    </edge>
