    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MINERALIZATION">
      <data key="d3">184.0</data>
      <data key="d4">**MINERALIZATION and TENEBRIO MOLITOR (Mealworms):**  
Tenebrio molitor, commonly known as mealworms, play a significant role in the mineralization of various types of plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), and low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Through their metabolic activities and the action of their gut microbiota, mealworms are capable of breaking down these plastics into simpler compounds, primarily converting them into carbon dioxide (CO2). This process not only demonstrates their ability to biodegrade plastics but also highlights their potential to reduce the environmental impact of plastic waste. In some cases, the mineralization process also results in the incorporation of plastic-derived carbon into the mealworms' biomass, such as lipids. Overall, Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the mineralization of plastics into CO2 and other inorganic compounds, showcasing their role in the biodegradation of synthetic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the mineralization of ingested plastics, converting them into CO2 during the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms contribute to the mineralization of polystyrene into CO2, demonstrating their role in plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e</data>
    </edge>
