    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CLOSTRIDIUM">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Clostridium bacteria are part of the gut microbiome of mealworms, aiding in their digestion.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium bacteria are stimulated in the gut of Tenebrio molitor when fed high-nutrient diets, affecting their metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium is a bacterial genus identified in the gut microbiome of mealworms, particularly in Diet 3.&lt;SEP&gt;Clostridium bacteria in the digestive system of Tenebrio molitor larvae are negatively correlated with the PS diet and nitrogen metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7</data>
