    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DIET 3">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Diet 3 (high bran:polystyrene ratio) was used to study the effects on Tenebrio molitor's gut microbiota and polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Diet 3 is used as a control to assess the metabolism of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae without hydration.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MICROBIOME">
      <data key="d3">43.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics such as polystyrene (PS) and low-density polyethylene (LDPE).&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of styrene and its derivatives.&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The microbiome of mealworms is crucial for their ability to degrade polyethylene and adapt to different diets.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="WATER">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Water is added to experimental diets to study its effect on the growth and PS degradation capabilities of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MICROFLORA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The microflora in the intestines of Tenebrio molitor larvae may play a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EXPANDED PS (EPS)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Expanded PS (EPS) is the material being tested for biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ROLLED BARLEY">
      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Rolled barley is a key component of the control diet provided to Tenebrio molitor larvae, influencing their growth and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;Rolled barley is used as a control diet for Tenebrio molitor larvae in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Rolled barley was used as part of the diet for mealworm larvae to evaluate their growth and PS biodegradation efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ETHANOL (ETOH)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Ethanol is used to sterilize the external surface of Tenebrio molitor larvae before collecting internal samples for microflora analysis.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CLIMATE-CONTROLLED ROOM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">A climate-controlled room is used to maintain optimal environmental conditions for Tenebrio molitor larvae during biodegradation experiments.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYPROPYLENE (PP) CONTAINERS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polypropylene (PP) containers are used to house Tenebrio molitor larvae during the biodegradation experiments.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LARVAE SURVIVAL">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Larvae survival is monitored to assess the impact of different diets on Tenebrio molitor larvae during biodegradation experiments.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ERWINIA OLEA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Erwinia olea is more abundant in the gut of Tenebrio molitor fed with polystyrene, suggesting its involvement in biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LACTOCOCCUS LACTIS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lactococcus lactis is identified in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, potentially contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LACTOCOCCUS GARVIAE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lactococcus garviae is found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, possibly aiding in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MOISTURE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The growth and development of Tenebrio molitor are influenced by moisture levels, as studied in controlled environments.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENTOMOREMEDIATION">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor is a key organism in entomoremediation, the process of using insects to biodegrade plastics and other waste materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is used in entomoremediation to degrade plastic waste, offering a potential solution to plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="THERMAL BUILDING INSULATION POLYSTYRENE FOAM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Thermal building insulation polystyrene foam can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor, reducing its environmental impact.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KITCHEN SPONGE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kitchen sponge (PU1) can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor, contributing to waste management solutions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="COMMERCIAL THERMAL INSULATION FOAM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Commercial thermal insulation foam (PU2) can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor, offering a potential solution to plastic waste pollution.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STYRENE-BUTADIENE RUBBER (SBR)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR), showcasing its potential in plastic waste management</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="TIRES CRUMBS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade tire crumbs, contributing to the management of rubber waste</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CHITOSAN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can be a source of chitosan, which is used in UV-protective packaging</data>
