      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can promote the growth of Bifidobacteriaceae in the intestines of mice</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LACTOBACILLACEAE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can promote the growth of Lactobacillaceae in the intestines of mice</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="NPK FERTILIZERS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor frass can be used as a substitute or additive for NPK fertilizers</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="BIOGAS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor frass can be used to produce biogas through anaerobic digestion</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="UV-PROTECTIVE PACKAGING">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Chitosan derived from Tenebrio molitor can be used to produce UV-protective packaging</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYURETHANE 1 (PU1)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae consumed and degraded polyurethane 1 (PU1), with a significant reduction in mass observed during the experiment.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYURETHANE 2 (PU2)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae consumed and degraded polyurethane 2 (PU2), showing a higher percentage of utilization compared to other plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ZOPHOBAS MORIO">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Both Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas morio are insects from the same family (Tenebrionidae) and are studied for their ability to degrade plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CORN FLOUR">
      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Corn flour enhances the plastic consumption rate of Tenebrio molitor, improving their ability to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour is used as a food additive to enhance the degradation efficiency of plastics like PS by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour improves the consumption and biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by Tenebrio molitor larvae, supporting their survival and growth.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MITOCHONDRIAL DNA">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms' mitochondrial DNA is studied for epigenetic modifications caused by polyurethane (PU) as a sole source of feed.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CANNIBALISM">
      <data key="d3">38.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cannibalism among mealworms affects their survival and degradation rates of PE substrates.&lt;SEP&gt;Cannibalism among mealworms can reduce plastic consumption rates when larvae and adults are kept together.&lt;SEP&gt;Cannibalism is observed in Tenebrio molitor larvae, particularly in the PE-reg diet, leading to high mortality rates.&lt;SEP&gt;Cannibalism is observed in Tenebrio molitor larvae, particularly in the PE-reg group, where pupae are preyed upon.&lt;SEP&gt;Cannibalism behavior in Tenebrio molitor larvae affects their survival rates during experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Cannibalism in Tenebrio molitor larvae occurs due to insufficient food or nutrients, impacting their survival.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PU1">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PU1, a soft polyurethane, is less efficiently degraded by mealworms due to its flexible and elastic properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can consume and degrade PU1, a specific type of polyurethane plastic.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PU2">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PU2, a rigid polyurethane, is more efficiently degraded by mealworms due to its brittle and stiff properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor can consume and degrade PU2, another specific type of polyurethane plastic.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYURETHANE FOAM">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polyurethane foam can induce epigenetic modifications in Tenebrio molitor during its metamorphic stages.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade polyurethane foam, achieving a 35% degradation rate in 17 days, contributing to environmental waste reduction.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYSTYRENE DIET">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae are studied for their ability to survive and grow on a polystyrene diet, contributing to plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DYNAMIC ENERGY BUDGET (DEB) MODEL">
      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The DEB model is used to analyze the effects of polystyrene diet on the growth, development, and survival of mealworms, providing insights into their role in biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The DEB model is used to analyze the growth and metabolism of mealworms, particularly when exposed to polystyrene, to understand their energy budget and physiological responses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dynamic Energy Budget (DEB) model is used to analyze the effects of a polystyrene diet on Tenebrio molitor larval growth and survival.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CRONOBACTER SAKAZAKII">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cronobacter sakazakii, a potential EPS-degrading bacterium, shows increased population in mealworms fed with EPS, indicating its role in EPS degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LACTOCOCCUS GARVIEAE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lactococcus garvieae, another potential EPS-degrading bacterium, shows increased population in mealworms fed with EPS, indicating its role in EPS degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. YT2">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Exiguobacterium sp. YT2, a known EPS-degrading bacterium, is found in the guts of mealworms and contributes to the biodegradation of EPS.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2, found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EPS FOAM">
      <data key="d3">31.0</data>
      <data key="d4">EPS foam is consumed and biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor mealworms, with a significant portion converted into CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed EPS foam show non-lethal effects but reduced growth and reproductive performance compared to standard diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed with EPS foam show higher productivity measures compared to XPS foam, indicating differences in the physical and chemical properties of the foams.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are used to study the biodegradation of EPS foam, with gut microbes playing a significant role in depolymerization.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SYMBIOTIC MICROORGANISMS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Symbiotic microorganisms in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae are essential for the biodegradation of EPS and LDPE.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CANNIBALIZATION">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cannibalization occurs in Tenebrio molitor larvae when they are fed only EPS or LDPE, indicating a lack of necessary nutrients.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PE-1">
      <data key="d3">37.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PE-1 is a polyethylene feedstock used to study the biodegradation capabilities of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;PE-1 is a type of LDPE foam consumed and degraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;PE-1 is consumed and biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae consume and depolymerize PE-1, a sample of low-density polyethylene (LDPE).&lt;SEP&gt;PE-1 is partially digested and depolymerized by Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to its biodegradation</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PE-2">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PE-2 is another type of LDPE foam consumed and degraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae&lt;SEP&gt;PE-2 is consumed and biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, showing similar patterns to PE-1.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae consume and depolymerize PE-2, another sample of low-density polyethylene (LDPE).</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PUPAE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
