    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PROCESSED POLYSTYRENE (PSR)">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can biodegrade processed polystyrene (PSr), which has undergone multiple processing cycles.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms were tested for their ability to biodegrade processed polystyrene (PSr), a modified form of PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Processed polystyrene (PSr) caused moderate mass loss in mealworms, suggesting limited degradation potential.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd</data>
    </edge>
