      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="BACILLUS SP. PELW2042">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacillus sp. PELW2042 was isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, indicating a symbiotic relationship in HDPE degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. PELW2042 was isolated from the guts of Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating a symbiotic relationship in the biodegradation of polyethylene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="HDPE">
      <data key="d3">108.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) can degrade HDPE, reducing its mass by up to 32% after one month of exposure.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor consumes HDPE, which affects its gut microbial diversity and plays a role in the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor is studied for its ability to degrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE) through its gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are involved in the biodegradation of HDPE, with specific consumption rates and residual PE percentages observed.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are used to biodegrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE) microplastics, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrade HDPE, leading to oxidative stress and physiological responses.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade HDPE, but the rate of degradation is slower compared to LDPE and LLDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade HDPE, generating different metabolic intermediates during the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade HDPE, contributing to the reduction of environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor has been observed to partially biodegrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE), although at a slower rate compared to LDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae biodegrade HDPE, but its high crystallinity and stability result in limited depolymerization&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade HDPE microplastics, although the process is less efficient compared to LDPE&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can depolymerize HDPE, though to a limited extent, resulting in an increase in molecular weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can ingest and biodegrade HDPE, though it is more resistant to depolymerization compared to LDPE and LLDPE.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae were tested for their ability to degrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE)</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7</data>
    </edge>
