      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PP_{575}">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PP_{575} is consumed and degraded by mealworms, demonstrating their ability to biodegrade pelletized PP.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="COMMERCIAL PP MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms consume and biodegrade commercial PP microplastics, reducing their mass and molecular weight over time.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SPECIFIC PP CONSUMPTION RATE (SPCR)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The specific PP consumption rate (SPCR) measures the rate at which Tenebrio molitor larvae consume polypropylene, indicating their efficiency in biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SURVIVAL RATE (SR)">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Survival rate (SR) is used to measure the ability of Tenebrio molitor larvae to survive when fed LDPE foams&lt;SEP&gt;The survival rate (SR) of Tenebrio molitor larvae is higher when fed polypropylene, indicating its role as a carbon and energy source.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="WEIGHT CHANGE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Weight change in Tenebrio molitor larvae is monitored to assess the impact of polypropylene consumption on their growth and survival.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ATP-BINDING CASSETTE (ABC) TRANSPORTER">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae express ATP-binding cassette (ABC) transporter pathways to facilitate the importation of PP degradation intermediates for further metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="QUORUM SENSING">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Quorum sensing pathways are enriched in PP-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, aiding in the coordination of microbial activities during plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="NITROGEN METABOLISM PATHWAY (KO00910)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The nitrogen metabolism pathway (KO00910) is enriched in PP-fed Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating nitrogen fixation during plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DIAZOTROPHS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae rely on diazotrophs (nitrogen-fixing bacteria) to supplement their nitrogen supply when fed a nitrogen-deficient diet of PP.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="TRANSCRIPTOMIC ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Transcriptomic analysis was used to study the gene expression changes in Tenebrio molitor larvae when exposed to polypropylene, revealing their biodegradation capabilities</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DEGS (DIFFERENTIALLY EXPRESSED GENES)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Differentially expressed genes (DEGs) in Tenebrio molitor larvae show adaptive responses to polypropylene diets, indicating changes in gene expression related to plastic degradation</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MRPS (MULTIDRUG RESISTANCE PROTEINS)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Multidrug resistance proteins (MRPs) in Tenebrio molitor larvae help reduce metabolic pressure caused by plastic diets, aiding in survival under nutrient-deficient conditions</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SIGNAL TRANSDUCTION GENES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Signal transduction genes in Tenebrio molitor larvae help adapt to nutrient-deficient conditions caused by polypropylene diets</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYETHER-POLYURETHANE FOAM">
      <data key="d3">32.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyether-polyurethane foam, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyether-polyurethane foam, impacting their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade polyether-polyurethane foam, with significant effects on their gut microbiome.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PLASTIC MARINE DEBRIS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae contribute to the degradation of plastic marine debris, aiding in waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYSTYRENE WASTES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade polystyrene wastes, contributing to environmental remediation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GUT METABOLOME">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The gut metabolome of Tenebrio molitor plays a role in the biodegradation of plastics like polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="HOST GENES">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Host genes in Tenebrio molitor are studied to understand their role in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Host genes in mealworms are upregulated during PET depolymerization and metabolism, indicating their essential role in the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Host genes in mealworms are upregulated during PET depolymerization and metabolism, indicating their essential role in the biodegradation process.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="INTESTINAL MICROBIOTA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The intestinal microbiota of Tenebrio molitor shifts when consuming plastics like polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DIAZOTROPHIC COMMUNITY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The diazotrophic community in Tenebrio molitor may play a role in plastic biodegradation and nitrogen metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LACTOCOCCUS">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lactococcus bacteria are found in the gut of mealworms, contributing to their digestive processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Lactococcus is a key bacterium associated with the degradation of polyurethane in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PARACLOSTRIDIUM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Paraclostridium may contribute to the degradation of polyurethane in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KOSAKONIA">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kosakonia may be involved in the degradation of polyurethane in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
