    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="BIO4PURT PROJECT">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The BIO4Purt Project supports research on the ecological transition, including the study of polyurethane biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYMER DEGRADATION">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polymer degradation is facilitated by Tenebrio molitor larvae through their gut microbiome and enzymatic activity.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MEALWORM PASTE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworm paste is derived from Tenebrio molitor and is explored as an alternative protein source for food and feed.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LONG-TERM EFFECT">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The long-term effect of polystyrene feeding on yellow mealworms is studied to assess its impact on their growth and transcriptomic response.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MICROPLASTICS (MPS)">
      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics (MPs) are ingested by Tenebrio molitor larvae, leading to studies on their biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading microplastics, providing a potential solution for managing plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae experience oxidative stress and increased antioxidant enzyme activity when exposed to microplastics during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade microplastics (MPs) such as PE, PP, and PS through the action of gut microorganisms and enzymes.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLY(BUTYLENE ADIPATE-CO-TEREPHTHALATE) (PBAT)">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can degrade PBAT and use its intermediates as an energy supplement, demonstrating their plastic-degrading capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade and assimilate PBAT for energy supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="METABOLIC DYSBIOSIS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae may experience metabolic dysbiosis due to exposure to micro(nano)plastics during biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ANTIOXIDANT ENZYME ACTIVITIES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Antioxidant enzyme activities are used to evaluate oxidative stress responses in Tenebrio molitor larvae during plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KAPLAN-MEIER SURVIVAL ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kaplan-Meier survival analysis was used to assess the survival rates of Tenebrio molitor larvae over a 6-week period</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SUPEROXIDE DISMUTASE (SOD)">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">SOD is measured to evaluate oxidative stress levels in Tenebrio molitor larvae exposed to polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae show increased superoxide dismutase (SOD) activity in response to oxidative stress caused by microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GLUTATHIONE-S-TRANSFERASE (GST)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae exhibit increased glutathione-S-transferase (GST) activity to alleviate oxidative damage caused by microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CATALASE (CAT)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae show increased catalase (CAT) activity in response to oxidative stress induced by microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MALONDIALDEHYDE (MDA)">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">MDA is measured to assess oxidative damage in Tenebrio molitor larvae exposed to polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae exhibit increased malondialdehyde (MDA) levels, indicating lipid peroxidation and oxidative damage caused by microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CORN STRAW">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can degrade corn straw, a natural lignocellulose material, through their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae consume and partially digest corn straw, breaking down its cellulose, hemicellulose, and lignin components</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="VANCOMYCIN">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Vancomycin suppresses the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae, impacting their biodegradation capabilities&lt;SEP&gt;Vancomycin, in combination with other antibiotics, is used to eliminate gut microbes in mealworms, affecting their plastic degradation capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="AMPICILLIN">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Ampicillin inhibits the gut flora of Tenebrio molitor larvae, reducing their ability to degrade polystyrene&lt;SEP&gt;Ampicillin is used to suppress gut microbiota in mealworms, impacting their ability to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Ampicillin suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, affecting PET biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Ampicillin suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, affecting PET biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </edge>
