      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The inbreeding farm in Lublin provided the Tenebrio molitor larvae used in the study.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PACKAGING MATERIAL (PSP)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms were used to assess the biodegradation of packaging material (PSP), a type of polystyrene used in food packaging.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GUT MICROBIOMES">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut microbiomes in Tenebrio molitor larvae are studied to understand their role in the biodegradation of microplastics (MPs) and their correlation with the aging index of MPs.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiomes of mealworms synergistically assist in the biodegradation of PET intermediates and provide nitrogen sources.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ERYTHROMYCIN">
      <data key="d3">21.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Erythromycin is tested for its ability to inhibit gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor during biodegradation studies&lt;SEP&gt;Erythromycin, in combination with other antibiotics, suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, affecting PET biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CHLORAMPHENICOL">
      <data key="d3">21.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Chloramphenicol is tested for its ability to inhibit gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor during biodegradation studies&lt;SEP&gt;Chloramphenicol suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, impacting their ability to degrade PET.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="TETRACYCLINE">
      <data key="d3">21.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tetracycline is tested for its ability to inhibit gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor during biodegradation studies&lt;SEP&gt;Tetracycline suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, reducing their ability to degrade PET.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KANAMYCIN">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kanamycin suppresses gut bacteria in mealworms, influencing their ability to degrade PET.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PET_{100}">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PET_{100} is a low molecular weight PET polymer used in biodegradation studies with mealworms.</data>
