      <data key="d6">chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="HFIP">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">HFIP is used to analyze the residual PET content in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae, aiding in the study of PET biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="IDEONELLA SAKAIENSIS 201-F6">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae show a higher PET degradation rate compared to Ideonella sakaiensis 201-F6, highlighting their efficiency in plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ANTIBIOTIC SUPPRESSION">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Antibiotic suppression studies reveal that Tenebrio molitor larvae can depolymerize PET independently of gut microbes, indicating host-mediated degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
