      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Both Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus are insects capable of biodegrading different types of plastic waste, contributing to environmental pollution reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus are hypothesized to share similar mechanisms for PET biodegradation, suggesting a broader applicability of this process in darkling beetle larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
