      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Achromobacter sp. is a gut bacterium of Tenebrio molitor involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="NANOPOLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae can degrade nanopolystyrene through the action of their gut microbiota.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MIXTA TENEBRIONIS">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mixta tenebrionis is a novel bacterial strain isolated from the gut of plastic-eating mealworms, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mixta tenebrionis was isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, indicating a symbiotic relationship where the bacterium may contribute to the mealworm's ability to degrade plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KLEBSIELLA SP. WJ2020">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Klebsiella sp. WJ2020 was isolated from the intestines of Tenebrio molitor, indicating its role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CELLULOSIMICROBIUM SP. WJ2025">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cellulosimicrobium sp. WJ2025 was isolated from the intestines of Tenebrio molitor, indicating its role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EXTRUDED POLYSTYRENE (XPS)">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are fed XPS foam to investigate its biodegradation and its impact on their development and fecundity.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed XPS foam showed reduced growth and fecundity compared to those fed EPS foam, indicating differences in the effects of Styrofoam types.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MEALWORMS BREEDERS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms breeders cultivate Tenebrio molitor for economic purposes, such as protein production or waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STYROFOAM WASTE DEGRADATION">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms contribute to the degradation of Styrofoam waste, offering a biological solution for plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STUDY DESIGN">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The study design involves feeding mealworms with EPS and XPS foams to assess their survival, growth, and fecundity, providing insights into their potential for biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="FERMENTED CASSAVA YEASTS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fermented cassava yeasts are used as a standard diet for mealworms to compare the effects of EPS and XPS foams on their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="MEALWORMS FARM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The mealworms farm is the source of the Tenebrio molitor larvae used in the study to investigate the biodegradation of EPS and XPS foams.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PREPUPAL PERIOD">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The prepupal period of mealworms is measured to evaluate the impact of EPS and XPS foams on their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PUPATION PERIOD">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The pupation period of mealworms is measured to assess the effects of EPS and XPS foams on their development into pupae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="IMAGO WEIGHT">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Imago weight is measured to determine the impact of EPS and XPS foams on the fecundity of mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="FECUNDITY">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fecundity is measured by the number of eggs laid by mealworms after being fed EPS and XPS foams, indicating their reproductive capacity.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="XPS FOAM">
      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms fed XPS foam exhibit lower growth and reproductive performance, indicating the negative impact of this polystyrene type.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms fed with XPS foam exhibit lower productivity, potentially due to the presence of formaldehyde and other chemical differences.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="YEAST">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Yeast serves as a standard diet for mealworms, providing essential nutrients and resulting in better growth and reproduction compared to polystyrene-based diets.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </edge>
