    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE &amp; TECHNOLOGY">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Environmental Science &amp; Technology published studies on the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;The journal Environmental Science &amp; Technology published research on the role of mealworms in the biodegradation of polystyrene&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies published in Environmental Science &amp; Technology investigate the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LIPIDOMICS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lipidomics studies reveal changes in lipid profiles in mealworms fed with polystyrene, indicating metabolic stress.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PROTEIN ALTERATIONS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Protein alterations in mealworms fed with polystyrene suggest metabolic stress and reduced protein biomass.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="APOPTOSIS BIOMARKERS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Apoptosis biomarkers increase in mealworms fed with polystyrene, indicating cellular stress.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EXPANDED PS (EPS) FOAM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Expanded PS foam is studied for its biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor larvae, demonstrating their ability to metabolize this material.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
