      <data key="d4">Illumina sequencing is used to analyze the bacterial diversity in the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different diet conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PRINCIPAL COMPONENT ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Principal component analysis (PCA) is used to study the gut microbial community structure of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different diet conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="BRAY-CURTIS DISTANCE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bray-Curtis distance is used to analyze the community diversity distance in the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae based on different diets.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 is isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, indicating the role of mealworm gut microbiota in polystyrene biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="VINYL PLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can degrade various vinyl plastics, such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and polypropylene, despite their nitrogen-deficient nature.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STYRENE-BUTADIENE RUBBER">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can degrade styrene-butadiene rubber (SBR), contributing to plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="UP-RECYCLING">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms contribute to the up-recycling of plastic waste by converting it into valuable protein sources through biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enzymes secreted by Tenebrio molitor larvae and their gut microorganisms are crucial for the depolymerization and biodegradation of microplastics (MPs).&lt;SEP&gt;The digestive tract and symbiotic bacteria of mealworms produce enzymes that play a crucial role in the biodegradation of various materials, including plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GLUTARALDEHYDE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Glutaraldehyde is used to fix the intestines of mealworm larvae for further analysis.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ISOMYL ACETATE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Isomyl acetate is used in the precipitation step during the preparation of mealworm intestines for freeze-drying.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PALLADIUM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Palladium is used to coat freeze-dried mealworm intestines for observation under a scanning electron microscope.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SCANNING ELECTRON MICROSCOPE (SEM)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The SEM is used to observe the surface of freeze-dried mealworm intestines coated with palladium.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="VIRGIN PE FILM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Virgin PE film is used in biodegradation experiments with mealworms to assess their ability to degrade plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="AGED PE FILM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Aged PE film is used in biodegradation experiments with mealworms to assess their ability to degrade degraded plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="VIRGIN PS FOAM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Virgin PS foam is used in biodegradation experiments with mealworms to assess their ability to degrade plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="AGED PS FOAM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Aged PS foam is used in biodegradation experiments with mealworms to assess their ability to degrade degraded plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="AGED MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae consume and biodegrade aged microplastics, with changes in the gut microbial community facilitating the degradation process.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="TRANSCRIPTOMIC RESPONSE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Transcriptomic response is studied in mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) to understand the long-term effects of plastic feeding on their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GUT COMMUNITIES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut communities in Tenebrio molitor larvae are shaped by their diet and play a role in enhancing the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene (LDPE).</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="OXIDIZED INTERMEDIATES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae produce oxidized intermediates during the depolymerization of low-density polyethylene (LDPE), indicating a broad biodegradation pattern.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LDPE FOAMS">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LDPE foams are consumed and biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, contributing to plastic waste reduction&lt;SEP&gt;LDPE foams are used in studies to assess the biodegradation capacity of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LIGNOCELLULOSIC MATERIALS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae consume lignocellulosic materials, which may contribute to their ability to biodegrade plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="KANAMYCIN SULFATE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kanamycin sulfate is tested for its ability to inhibit gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor during biodegradation studies</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PENICILLIN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Penicillin is tested for its ability to inhibit gut bacteria in Tenebrio molitor during biodegradation studies</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LURIA-BERTANI (LB) MEDIUM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Luria-Bertani (LB) medium is used to culture gut bacteria from Tenebrio molitor during antibiotic suppression tests</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LDPE DEPOLYMERIZATION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LDPE depolymerization is facilitated by the digestive systems of Tenebrio molitor larvae, leading to the breakdown of LDPE into smaller molecular weight components</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SPECIFIC LDPE CONSUMPTION RATE (SPCR)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Specific LDPE consumption rate (SPCR) measures the amount of LDPE consumed by Tenebrio molitor larvae</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="EMULSIFYING FACTOR(S)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Emulsifying factors secreted by Tenebrio molitor larvae enhance the bioavailability of plastics and promote biodegradation by gut bacteria.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ACINETOBACTER SEPTICUS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Acinetobacter septicus is one of the symbiotic bacteria isolated from mealworms that contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENRICHMENT CULTURE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enrichment culture is used to isolate and increase the population of polystyrene-degrading bacteria from the intestines of mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DIGESTIVE BIOFRAGMENTATION MODEL">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The digestive biofragmentation model simulates the size-reduction process of plastic particles in the intestinal tract of Tenebrio molitor larvae, aiding in understanding plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GEL PERMEATION CHROMATOGRAPHY (GPC)">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">GPC analysis is used to confirm the depolymerization and biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="METABOLOME">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The metabolome of mealworms is reprogrammed during the biodegradation of polystyrene, with metabolic changes dependent on the molecular weight of the PS polymers.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="POLYLACTIDE (PLA)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can biodegrade polylactide, a biodegradable plastic, further demonstrating their role in plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="BRADFORD METHOD">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Bradford method was used to determine the protein concentration in mealworms, providing insights into their biochemical changes during plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ANTHRONE METHOD">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The anthrone method was used to measure hydrolyzed carbohydrates in mealworms, contributing to the study of their biochemical composition.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SULFO-PHOSPHO-VANILLIN ASSAY (SPVA)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The SPVA was used to quantify total lipids in mealworms, aiding in the analysis of their biochemical changes during plastic consumption.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ENTEROBACTERIACEAE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacteriaceae, including Citrobacter spp. and Kosakonia spp., colonize mealworm larvae fed plastics, contributing to their gut microbiome.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DEB MODEL">
      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The DEB model is applied to analyze the growth and reserve dynamics of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different feeding conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The DEB model is used to analyze the development and reserve dynamics of Tenebrio molitor larvae, particularly in relation to their ability to survive under food shortages and potential biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The DEB model is used to analyze the energy dynamics and physiological responses of Tenebrio molitor larvae under starvation and PS consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;The DEB model is used to analyze the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different feeding conditions, providing insights into their energy budget and life cycle.&lt;SEP&gt;The DEB model is used to analyze the growth and energy allocation of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different conditions, including exposure to PS.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STARVATION GROUPS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae are subjected to starvation conditions to study their survival and growth patterns.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PS LARGE GROUP">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Older and larger Tenebrio molitor larvae are fed polystyrene to assess their consumption and growth compared to smaller larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;The PS large group is used to study the effects of larger PS pieces on the degradation ability and survival of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PS + OAT GROUP">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae are fed a combination of polystyrene and oatmeal to study their growth and feeding behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The PS + oat group demonstrates the positive effects of oatmeal supplementation on the survival and PS degradation ability of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="LABORATORY CONDITIONS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae are reared under controlled laboratory conditions to study their growth and development.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="VITAMINS">
      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Vitamin supplementation supports the survival and enzymatic activity of Tenebrio molitor larvae, aiding in the degradation of PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamins are added to the diet of mealworms to study their impact on growth and survival when combined with polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamins, when supplemented in the diet, significantly improve the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="CONTROL SAMPLE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The control sample provides baseline data on the density and survival of Tenebrio molitor larvae under standard conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STARVATION GROUP">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The starvation group is used to study the effects of nutrient deprivation on the survival and PS degradation ability of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="PS + OAT. + VIT. GROUP">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The PS + oat. + vit. group shows the combined effects of oatmeal and vitamin supplementation on the survival and PS degradation ability of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="SURVIVAL CURVES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Survival curves are used to analyze the survival rates of Tenebrio molitor larvae under different feeding conditions, providing insights into their energetic costs.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DIETARY SUPPLEMENTS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Dietary supplements, such as oatmeal and vitamins, improve the survival and functioning of Tenebrio molitor larvae, enhancing their ability to degrade PS.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="STARCH">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Starch is a key dietary component that supports the growth and development of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="DEB MODEL PARAMETERS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">DEB model parameters are used to analyze the growth and energy dynamics of Tenebrio molitor larvae under various dietary conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="RESERVES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Reserves, such as triglycerides, are critical for the survival of mealworms during food deprivation, serving as a primary energy source.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="ALPHITOBIUS DIAPERINUS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Both Tenebrio molitor and Alphitobius diaperinus exhibit similar metabolic responses to food deprivation, particularly in triglyceride levels.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="TRIGLYCERIDES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Triglycerides are fat reserves in mealworms that serve as a primary energy source during food deprivation or starvation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR" target="GLYCOGEN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Glycogen is a carbohydrate reserve in mealworms that plays a role in sustaining the nervous system during food deprivation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
