    <edge source="ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">341.0</data>
      <data key="d4">**Polystyrene and Zophobas atratus (Superworms):**  

Zophobas atratus, commonly known as superworms, exhibit a remarkable ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene (PS), a widely used plastic in packaging and other applications. The larvae of Zophobas atratus can ingest, digest, and degrade polystyrene, significantly contributing to the breakdown of this plastic material. This biodegradation process is facilitated by the larvae's gut microbiome, which undergoes distinct changes during the degradation process. Specific bacterial strains, such as Pseudomonas aeruginosa DSM 50071, play a crucial role in breaking down polystyrene, highlighting the importance of gut bacteria in this process.  

Superworms have demonstrated higher efficiency in consuming and biodegrading polystyrene foam compared to other organisms, such as yellow mealworms. They exhibit the strongest consumption capacity and survival rate among organisms studied for polystyrene degradation, with the ability to depolymerize polystyrene into low-molecular-weight substances. However, their survival rates can be affected by nutrient limitations, which may influence the extent of biodegradation.  

The ability of Zophobas atratus to biodegrade polystyrene has important implications for plastic waste management and environmental cleanup. By breaking down polystyrene, these larvae contribute to the reduction of plastic pollution. However, the process may lead to the formation of microplastics, which still pose environmental challenges. Despite this, Zophobas atratus represents a promising biological tool for managing plastic waste, particularly in environments where polystyrene accumulation is a concern.  

Overall, the biodegradation of polystyrene by Zophobas atratus larvae, supported by their gut microbiome, offers a potential solution for reducing plastic waste and mitigating its environmental impact. Their unique capabilities position them as a key subject of study in the field of plastic biodegradation and environmental remediation.  

In summary, Zophobas atratus larvae are capable of biodegrading and mineralizing polystyrene through oxidative processes in their gut, with distinct changes in their gut microbiome during the process. This contributes to the reduction of plastic pollution, although it may also lead to the fragmentation of polystyrene into microplastics. Their potential in addressing plastic pollution makes them a significant focus in environmental remediation efforts.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-937d9d4e1671351e8e90f0bd2647f321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834</data>
