    <edge source="ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS" target="RESEARCH STUDY">
      <data key="d3">42.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Research studies explore the biodegradation capabilities of superworms when fed on polypropylene and other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;This research study focuses on the ability of Zophobas atratus to degrade and mineralize polystyrene, highlighting its potential for addressing plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study examines the role of Zophobas atratus in the depolymerization and biodegradation of polypropylene (PP).&lt;SEP&gt;This research study investigates the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) by Zophobas atratus larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies have explored the biodegradation capabilities of Zophobas atratus, particularly in relation to polypropylene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714</data>
    </edge>
