    <edge source="GALLERIA MELLONELLA" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">137.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Galleria mellonella (greater wax moth) can digest polystyrene, leading to changes in its gut microbiome composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella can chew and eat polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Greater wax moth larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, highlighting their role in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can biodegrade polystyrene, with their gut microbiome playing a significant role in the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can biodegrade polystyrene and styrofoam, with their gut microbiome playing a key role in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, aiding in the reduction of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Greater wax moth larvae (Galleria mellonella) can biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can degrade polystyrene, with specific gut bacteria playing a key role in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can biodegrade polystyrene due to their gut microbial flora.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae have been found to degrade polystyrene, with bacteria isolated from their guts playing a key role in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can degrade polystyrene, with changes in gut microbiota diversity observed after feeding on PS.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, similar to Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas aratus.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, similar to other insect larvae like Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus.&lt;SEP&gt;Galleria mellonella larvae can biodegrade polystyrene, with their gut microbiome playing a crucial role in the process.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85ab9c6af7915311ccbb4804160be5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd</data>
    </edge>
