      <data key="d3">60.0</data>
      <data key="d4">GPC analysis characterizes the molecular weight of residual PS after biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to determine the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene (PS) during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to measure changes in the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene during biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to measure the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene residues after degradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to measure the molecular weight reduction of polystyrene (PS) after biodegradation by superworms and yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to study changes in the molecular weight of polystyrene during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis reveals depolymerization patterns in polystyrene, showing molecular weight changes in the frass of mealworms&lt;SEP&gt;GPC analysis is used to measure the molecular weight of polystyrene (PS) in frass, indicating the extent of depolymerization during biodegradation.</data>
