      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain that can degrade polystyrene, demonstrating the role of gut bacteria in the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2, isolated from Tenebrio molitor larvae, is capable of degrading polystyrene, demonstrating the role of gut bacteria in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is involved in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene (PS), highlighting the role of gut bacteria in plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
