    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE (PS)" target="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polystyrene (PS) is the primary component of Styrofoam, which is consumed and degraded by superworms, greater wax moths, and yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam is a form of expanded polystyrene (EPS) foam, which is the primary material studied for biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam is a form of expanded polystyrene (PS) foam, which mealworms can biodegrade.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam is a form of polystyrene (PS) used in the experiment to study its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam is a form of expanded polystyrene (PS) used as a feedstock in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrofoam is a form of expanded polystyrene (PS) foam, which is the focus of biodegradation studies.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE (PS)" target="GEL PERMEATION CHROMATOGRAPHY (GPC)">
      <data key="d3">68.0</data>
      <data key="d4">GPC is used to analyze changes in the molecular weight of polystyrene (PS) after biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC is used to analyze the molecular weight and distribution of PS samples extracted with DMF.&lt;SEP&gt;Gel permeation chromatography (GPC) is used to assess changes in the molecular weight of polystyrene during biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Gel permeation chromatography (GPC) is used to characterize polystyrene (PS) residues in the frass of mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC is used to analyze the molecular weight and distribution of polystyrene during its depolymerization and degradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Gel permeation chromatography is used to analyze the molecular weights of residual polystyrene polymers in the frass of Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC is used to measure molecular weight changes in degraded polystyrene films&lt;SEP&gt;Gel permeation chromatography (GPC) is used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene (PS) in biodegradation studies.&lt;SEP&gt;GPC was used to analyze changes in the molecular weight of PS polymers ingested by mealworms</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
