      <data key="d3">24.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Pseudomonas aeruginosa contributes to the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by causing surface alterations and oxidative changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa is capable of degrading crude oil and producing biosurfactants, which may enhance polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa is capable of breaking down polystyrene (PS), contributing to its biodegradation.</data>
