    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE (PS)" target="GUT BACTERIA">
      <data key="d3">43.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut bacteria in T. obscurus and T. molitor are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS), with their suppression leading to a loss of PS depolymerization capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules and contributing to mineralization.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by breaking down its structure and contributing to its mineralization.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms play a crucial role in the degradation of polystyrene (PS), as shown by their suppression using antibiotics.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria isolated from Tenebrio molitor larvae are tested for their ability to grow on polystyrene, indicating their role in biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
