    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOTA" target="MEALWORMS">
      <data key="d3">80.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms host gut microbiota that play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polyethylene (PE).&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms rely on their gut microbiota to biodegrade polystyrene, highlighting the symbiotic relationship between the organism and its microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of plastics, aiding in the breakdown of complex polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, as their suppression by gentamicin inhibits degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms is essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) and other plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, including polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms play an essential role in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms plays a significant role in the biodegradation of polystyrene but has a lesser role in cellulose degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOTA" target="LACTOBACILLUS SP.">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lactobacillus sp. modulates the gut microbiota of swine, improving gut health and overall well-being.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOTA" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">68.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut microbiota in insects plays a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, leading to the formation of PS oligomers.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbiota in mealworm larvae are essential for the biodegradation of polystyrene, as they form biofilms and physically alter the material.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut microbiota in mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor, including Bacillus and Exiguobacterium, plays a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms, including species like Serratia sp. and Rhodococcus sp., plays a key role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of insect larvae plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, with changes in microbial diversity observed after PS feeding.&lt;SEP&gt;Specific microbial taxa in the gut microbiota, such as Cronobacter, Kocuria, and Pseudomonas, are involved in the degradation of polystyrene&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms plays an essential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller molecules.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOTA" target="GENTAMICIN">
      <data key="d3">44.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gentamicin is used to suppress gut microbiota in insects, affecting their ability to degrade plastics like polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppresses gut microbiota in mealworms, negatively impacting their ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppresses the gut bacteria of mealworms, negatively impacting their ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppresses the gut microbiota of mealworms, negatively impacting their ability to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppresses the gut microbiota of mealworm larvae, negatively impacting their ability to degrade polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Gentamicin suppresses gut microbiota in T. molitor and Z. atratus, negatively impacting their ability to biodegrade polypropylene (PP).</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b</data>
    </edge>
