    <edge source="GUT MICROBIOTA" target="NITROGEN FIXATION">
      <data key="d3">41.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Nitrogen fixation by gut microbes synthesizes proteins needed by Tenebrio molitor larvae during the biodegradation of polypropylene&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of Tenebrio larvae has the potential to fix nitrogen biologically, helping to maintain nitrogen nutrition during PE degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms is responsible for nitrogen fixation, enabling the assimilation of atmospheric nitrogen.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms plays a role in nitrogen fixation, facilitated by diazotrophic bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut microbiota of mealworms, including nitrogen-fixing bacteria, plays a crucial role in enabling mealworms to survive on nitrogen-deficient diets like Styrofoam.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252</data>
    </edge>
