      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Spiroplasma is strongly associated with the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) in the gut microbiome of yellow mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Spiroplasma was found to be dominant in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with polypropylene (PP) foam plastics, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation.</data>
