    </edge>
    <edge source="MINERALIZATION" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">78.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mineralization is the process by which polystyrene is converted into CO2, facilitated by mealworms and their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineralization refers to the conversion of polystyrene into CO2 during degradation by superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is mineralized into CO2 by superworms, with up to 36.7% of ingested Styrofoam carbon being converted during the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is mineralized into CO2 by mealworms, with a significant portion of ingested PS converted into CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms converts it into CO2, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineralization of polystyrene into CO2 occurs during biodegradation by mealworms and superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Mineralization of polystyrene into CO2 occurs during its biodegradation by mealworms and their gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is mineralized into CO2 during the biodegradation process facilitated by mealworms and their gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is mineralized into CO2 by mealworms, indicating its biodegradation potential.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
    </edge>
