    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">360.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) have demonstrated a remarkable ability to biodegrade polystyrene (PS), a common plastic material, thereby contributing to the reduction of plastic waste and its environmental impact. This biodegradation process involves multiple stages, including chewing, microbial interaction, and enzymatic decomposition facilitated by the mealworms' gut microbiota. The gut bacteria of mealworms play a crucial role in breaking down polystyrene, with specific microorganisms and upregulated enzymes, such as Lac640, driving the oxidative digestive machinery required for degradation.

When mealworms consume polystyrene, they metabolize it, leading to the excretion of metabolites like fatty acids and cholesterol. This process not only degrades the plastic but also enriches the mealworms' gut microbiota with microorganisms involved in biodegradation. Research has shown that mealworms can mineralize polystyrene, transforming it into simpler compounds and reducing its persistence in the environment.

The ability of mealworms to biodegrade polystyrene has significant implications for plastic waste management. By isolating and studying the gut bacteria responsible for this process, scientists aim to develop innovative solutions for addressing plastic pollution. Mealworms are thus considered a key organism in biodegradation research, offering a natural and sustainable approach to mitigating the environmental impact of polystyrene waste.

Mealworms are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, as evidenced by mass loss measurements and biochemical changes in the mealworms. They can chew and degrade polystyrene, with their gut bacteria playing a crucial role in the biodegradation process. This capability suggests their potential role in plastic waste management and environmental remediation.

In summary, mealworms (*Tenebrio molitor*) are capable of degrading polystyrene through the action of their gut microorganisms, contributing to the breakdown of this environmental pollutant. Their ability to biodegrade and mineralize polystyrene highlights their potential as a natural solution for addressing plastic pollution and advancing environmental remediation efforts. Mealworms are fed polystyrene to study their ability to biodegrade and mineralize the plastic, further emphasizing their role in biodegradation and environmental solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, contributing to the reduction of plastic waste in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms biodegrade polystyrene (PS), leading to the generation of microplastics (MPs) during the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can digest polystyrene through a multi-stage process involving chewing, microbial interaction, and enzymatic decomposition.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f7a49f1c1e76d6e987e0aa499923d3f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ee089593160e720e507848fa8c917a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326aabc25dd967951a7845ea221532ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62</data>
