    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="GUT BACTERIA">
      <data key="d3">44.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the digestion of synthetic and natural polymers, such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and cellulose.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms are essential for the digestion of synthetic and natural polymers, such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and cellulose.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut bacteria of mealworms play an essential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Gut bacteria in mealworms play a critical role in the degradation of plastics, including polystyrene, by breaking down polymer chains.&lt;SEP&gt;The gut bacteria of mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, enabling depolymerization and mineralization.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
