    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="RESEARCH STUDY">
      <data key="d3">134.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Research studies have been conducted to investigate the ability of mealworms to consume and degrade various types of plastics, including polystyrene, polypropylene, and polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on mealworms and their ability to degrade plastics such as EPS, PE, and NPS.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms and the role of their gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on understanding the microbial and enzymatic changes in mealworms fed different types of waste.&lt;SEP&gt;This research study investigates the ubiquity of polystyrene degradation in mealworms from diverse global sources, using standardized protocols to assess PS degradation rates and mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on understanding the mechanisms of polystyrene degradation by mealworms and their gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the role of mealworms in the biodegradation of polystyrene and their potential to address plastic waste pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the role of mealworms in the biodegradation of HDPE&lt;SEP&gt;This research study focuses on the ability of mealworms to degrade and mineralize polystyrene, highlighting the role of gut microbiota.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on understanding the factors that influence mealworms' ability to consume and biodegrade EPS.&lt;SEP&gt;This research study investigates the role of mealworms in the biodegradation of plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;This research study focuses on the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms, exploring the role of their gut microbiome and the impact of bran as a co-diet.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on the ability of mealworms to degrade polystyrene and the role of their gut bacteria in this process.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the ability of mealworms to biodegrade polystyrene and the factors influencing this process&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on understanding the microbial and enzymatic changes in mealworms fed different types of waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04</data>
