      <data key="d4">Mealworms are studied for their ability to biodegrade LDPE, contributing to plastic waste management&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are tested for their ability to biodegrade LDPE, a common plastic material.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume LDPE, though consumption rates are lower compared to HIPS and EPS.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest LDPE, resulting in changes in molecular weight and chemical structure, indicating biodegradation&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms metabolize low-density polyethylene (LDPE) by breaking down its linear and branched chains, aiding in biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume LDPE, with varying effects on their weight and metabolism, indicating potential for biodegradation.</data>
