    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="MICROPLASTICS (MPS)">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms consume microplastics (MPS), which affects their survival, growth, and metamorphosis.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms consume microplastics, with older larvae showing greater consumption and degradation capabilities&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest microplastics during polystyrene biodegradation, which can induce gut epithelium damage and metabolic dysbiosis.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="OXIDATION">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms oxidize microplastics, modifying their functional groups and contributing to their degradation</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="TOXICOLOGICAL ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d3">76.0</data>
      <data key="d4">A toxicological assessment was conducted to evaluate the oxidative stress and damage in mealworms caused by ingesting microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms are used in a toxicological assessment to study the effects of microplastics on their survival, growth, and metamorphosis.&lt;SEP&gt;The study evaluates the toxicological effects of microplastic consumption on mealworm survival, growth, and metamorphosis&lt;SEP&gt;The biochemical characteristics of mealworms, such as protein, sugar, and lipid content, were assessed to determine the effects of feeding on polystyrene materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicological assessment evaluates the safety and effects of mealworms consuming EPS and other materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms' viability and mass changes are monitored as part of a toxicological assessment when they consume plastics lacking essential nutrients.&lt;SEP&gt;The study assesses the viability and mass changes of mealworms to determine the toxicological effects of plastic consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicological assessments have been conducted to evaluate the effects of plastic consumption on mealworms, including viability rates and mass changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicological assessments are conducted to evaluate the safety of mealworms and their ability to degrade polystyrene without adverse effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Toxicological assessment is necessary to evaluate the effects of microplastics on mealworms, including potential physical damage and reduced physiological performance.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </edge>
