    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d3">236.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) have demonstrated a remarkable ability to biodegrade Styrofoam, a form of expanded polystyrene (PS), which is a major environmental pollutant. Through their consumption and degradation of Styrofoam, mealworms contribute significantly to plastic waste management and environmental pollution mitigation. The biodegradation process involves the mealworms chewing and ingesting Styrofoam, which is then broken down by their gut microbiota. This process converts Styrofoam into biomass, carbon dioxide (CO2), and fecula, effectively reducing its mass and molecular weight. 

Studies have shown that mealworms can utilize Styrofoam as their sole diet, highlighting their adaptability to nitrogen-deficient plastic diets. The efficiency of this biodegradation process is further enhanced when additional nutrients are introduced into the environment. The gut bacteria of mealworms play a crucial role in this degradation, enabling the mineralization of Styrofoam into CO2 and other byproducts. 

Mealworms' ability to degrade Styrofoam offers a promising solution for managing this type of plastic waste, contributing to environmental remediation and reducing the accumulation of non-hydrolyzable vinyl plastics in ecosystems. Their role in the biodegradation of Styrofoam has been extensively studied, underscoring their potential as a natural tool for addressing plastic pollution. Overall, mealworms represent a significant biological agent in the fight against environmental pollution caused by expanded polystyrene materials like Styrofoam.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can biodegrade Styrofoam, a type of expanded polystyrene, through the action of their gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest and degrade Styrofoam, a type of expanded polystyrene, contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556</data>
    </edge>
