      <data key="d6">chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="ARDUINO DEVICES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Arduino devices were used to monitor the environmental conditions for mealworms during the study.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="CINNAMON POWDER">
      <data key="d3">5.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cinnamon powder has no significant effect on the consumption of polystyrene by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">5</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="SUCROSE">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Sucrose enhances the consumption of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms, optimizing the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Sucrose increases the consumption of polystyrene by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="PS BALLS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PS balls are consumed by mealworms, contributing to their biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-671dc96f9c648fdc6d21397c515d171d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="ZERO-WASTE CIRCULAR ECONOMY">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are utilized in a zero-waste circular economy to address plastic waste and food production challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms contribute to a zero-waste circular economy by degrading polystyrene and producing frass for sustainable agriculture.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">80.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms can biodegrade microplastics like PE, PS, and PVC, but this process induces oxidative stress and physiological damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume and metabolize various microplastics, including PS, PVC, and LDPE, contributing to their biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics are found in the frass of mealworms, indicating partial depolymerization of polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can degrade microplastics, contributing to the reduction of plastic pollution in the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms generate microplastics as a byproduct of incomplete polyethylene degradation, raising environmental concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can interact with microplastics, potentially breaking them down into smaller particles or metabolizing them.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms contribute to the formation of microplastics by fragmenting ingested PS and LDPE during biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can ingest and excrete microplastics, but undigested particles may cause physical damage and reduced nutrient uptake.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest and biodegrade microplastics, but residual plastic particles remain in their intestines, with PVC being the most persistent.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms ingest and biodegrade microplastics, leading to oxidative stress and damage, as evidenced by increased ROS, SOD, and MDA levels.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="TABLE SUCROSE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Table sucrose enhances the consumption of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms, optimizing the biodegradation process.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16</data>
    </edge>
