    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="HIGH-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (HDPE)">
      <data key="d3">51.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworms are tested for their ability to consume and degrade high-density polyethylene (HDPE), contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume high-density polyethylene (HDPE), but it causes significant mass reduction and has less branching, making it less bioresistant.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume high-density polyethylene (HDPE), leaving visible marks and holes in the plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume high-density polyethylene, but it results in significant mass loss in the initial stages&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume high-density polyethylene, but the consumption rate is slower than for other plastics&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms consume high-density polyethylene, but at a much lower rate compared to polystyrene and polypropylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms have been tested for their ability to consume high-density polyethylene (HDPE), with varying success rates.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="MIDGUT IMAGING">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Midgut imaging has been used to study the digestion process of plastics in mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORMS" target="MOLARITY AND FUNCTIONAL GROUPS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Analysis of molarity and functional groups has been conducted to understand the depolymerization of plastics after consumption by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
