    <edge source="RESEARCH STUDY" target="POLYSTYRENE">
      <data key="d3">146.0</data>
      <data key="d4">A research study has been conducted since the 1970s to explore the biodegradation of polystyrene by microorganisms and fungi.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on understanding the biodegradation process of polystyrene and its implications for reducing plastic waste pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the biodegradation of polystyrene by yellow mealworms, addressing environmental concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor and its gut microbiome, offering potential solutions for plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the mechanisms by which polystyrene is biodegraded by mealworms and their gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the biodegradation of polystyrene using Tenebrio molitor homogenates, contributing to understanding plastic degradation mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms, revealing a new fate for plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is a key subject of research studies exploring biodegradation and solutions to plastic waste pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies focus on understanding the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor and its gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies investigate the sources, behavior, and impacts of polystyrene in the marine environment, as well as its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Research studies focus on the recycling and biodegradation of polystyrene to address environmental concerns.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study by Yang et al. (2015a, 2015b) focuses on the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae, addressing environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study explores the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae and the role of their gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study focuses on identifying microbial species associated with polystyrene-fed insects and their role in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigates the effects of polystyrene on the gut microbial community of A. diaperinus larvae and its biodegradation potential.&lt;SEP&gt;The research study investigated the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor, contributing to environmental pollution mitigation strategies.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e540abd667582c77f4d2222836147ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98a6f770f1d3a35f8611c5f2516c1e08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
