    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="SUPERWORM">
      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Superworm (Zophobas atratus) can biodegrade polystyrene through its gut microbiome.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworm larvae are being investigated for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene, offering a potential solution to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms are capable of degrading polystyrene (PS) through the action of their gut bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms consume polystyrene (PS) but experience significant weight loss due to insufficient nutrition from a plastic-only diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms (Zophobas atratus) are capable of degrading Styrofoam, contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms have a higher polystyrene consumption rate compared to yellow mealworms, indicating their efficiency in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworm's gut microbes have the highest ability to degrade polystyrene into low-molecular-weight substances.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms can digest polystyrene, leading to changes in their gut microbiome composition.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="YELLOW MEALWORM">
      <data key="d3">71.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The yellow mealworm's gut microbiome responds to diet shifts during the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) are studied for their ability to biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to environmental solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are capable of degrading polystyrene (PS) through the action of their gut bacteria and fungi.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms consume polystyrene (PS) and show slight weight increases, indicating better adaptation to plastic diets compared to superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, with their gut microbiome adapting to diet shifts.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can survive on a sole diet of polystyrene, but their consumption rate is lower than that of superworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm shows higher efficiency in degrading polystyrene, as evidenced by lower PS content in its frass and unique degradation peaks.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworms can digest polystyrene, leading to changes in their gut microbiome composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Yellow mealworm larvae can biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to the reduction of plastic waste in the environment.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe</data>
