    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="OXIDATION">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Oxidation is a key process in the degradation of polystyrene, as detected by FTIR spectroscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidation occurs on the surface of polystyrene films during degradation, evidenced by the formation of hydroxyl groups and carbon-oxygen bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) undergoes oxidation in the guts of superworms and yellow mealworms, contributing to its biodegradation.</data>
