      <data key="d3">57.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Klebsiella oxytoca is capable of biodegrading polystyrene with a weight loss of 12.97 ± 1.05% over 60 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca is involved in the degradation of polystyrene, potentially using it as a carbon source.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca strains are identified and studied for their potential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca strains are studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene, contributing to biodegradation research.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca strains isolated from the guts of Tenebrio molitor are linked to the degradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella oxytoca, isolated from the gut of mealworms, is involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
