    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">83.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics can originate from the breakdown of polystyrene, contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics can result from the breakdown of polystyrene, posing environmental and health risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene can degrade into microplastics, which are persistent environmental pollutants affecting marine and terrestrial ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene contributes to the formation of microplastics, which are small plastic particles that pollute the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene can degrade into microplastics, which are persistent environmental pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene fragments contribute to the formation of microplastics, which accumulate in ecosystems and pose ecological risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene degradation can reduce the accumulation of microplastics in the environment&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene (PS) is fragmented into microplastics (MPs) during biodegradation by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene can break down into microplastics, contributing to environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is a major source of microplastics, which are subject to biodegradation by organisms like mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
