    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="STYRENE MONOMERS">
      <data key="d3">65.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polystyrene is composed of styrene monomers, which are more susceptible to biodegradation than the polymer itself&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is composed of styrene monomers, which are more susceptible to biodegradation than the polymer itself.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are the building blocks of polystyrene and are susceptible to biodegradation&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are the building blocks of polystyrene, which are released during the biodegradation process by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are the chemical components of polystyrene, which can be biodegraded under certain conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are the building blocks of polystyrene and are susceptible to biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are components of polystyrene that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are the building blocks of polystyrene and are more biodegradable than the polymer itself.&lt;SEP&gt;Styrene monomers are components of polystyrene that can be biodegraded.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
