    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="ZOPHOBAS MORIO">
      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Zophobas morio (superworm) can digest polystyrene, leading to changes in its gut microbiome composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio can consume polystyrene, but its nutritional value remains unaffected by this diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio is capable of degrading polystyrene, similar to other plastic-eating insects.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio, or superworms, are studied for their ability to consume polystyrene and its impact on their nutritional value and oxidative stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio consumes polystyrene, impacting its nutritional value and oxidative stress parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio larvae are studied for their ability to degrade polystyrene, similar to Tenebrio molitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio, like Tenebrio molitor, can consume polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.</data>
