      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The wax moth (Galleria mellonella) can chew and eat polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Wax Moth larvae exhibit elevated Vitamin B6 metabolism when exposed to PS, indicating a specific metabolic response to this plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Wax Moth larvae were exposed to PS to assess its effects on metabolism and larval weight.</data>
