    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="PSEUDOMONAS">
      <data key="d3">39.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Pseudomonas is found in the gut of mealworms and may play a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS).&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas is significantly more abundant in polystyrene-fed samples and is associated with the degradation of polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas plays a role in the degradation of polystyrene in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas species were significantly over-represented in polystyrene (PS) samples, suggesting their role in PS degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas was overrepresented in PS samples, indicating its potential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
