    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="MEALWORM">
      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworm larvae exhibit metabolic activity when exposed to polystyrene, suggesting a role in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) can biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms can consume and degrade polystyrene, which affects their survival and growth rates&lt;SEP&gt;Mealworms, including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscura, are capable of biodegrading polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
