      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Plastic-eating waxworms (Galleria mellonella) can biodegrade polystyrene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic-eating waxworms can biodegrade polystyrene, with their gut bacteria playing a crucial role in the process.&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic-eating waxworms can degrade polyethylene, a synthetic polymer, with the help of gut bacteria, suggesting a similar potential for polystyrene.</data>
