    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="ACHROMOBACTER XYLOSOXIDANS M9">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9 degrades polystyrene nanoplastics, reducing particle size and altering chemical composition, indicating its potential for bioremediation.&lt;SEP&gt;Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9 is capable of biodegrading polystyrene with a weight loss of 7% over 30 days.&lt;SEP&gt;Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9 is capable of degrading polystyrene and forming biofilms, as identified in mealworm intestines.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
