      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Achromobacter xylosidans M9 exhibits the highest efficacy in degrading polystyrene, achieving a 7% reduction in PS film weight.&lt;SEP&gt;Achromobacter xylosidans M9 is studied for its ability to biodegrade polystyrene, with research focusing on its enzymatic and genetic mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
