      <data key="d3">14.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 plays a role in the degradation of polystyrene, as identified in mealworm intestines.&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 produces lipases, esterases, and laccases, indicating its potential role in polystyrene degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d</data>
