      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Acinetobacter septicus has been shown to degrade polystyrene, indicating its role in the biodegradation process.&lt;SEP&gt;Acinetobacter septicus is one of the bacterial strains tested for its potential to degrade polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Acinetobacter septicus shows growth on agar and cracks in PS film over 14 days, indicating its role in polystyrene biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
