    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="A. TUMEFACIENS MA92">
      <data key="d3">42.0</data>
      <data key="d4">A. tumefaciens MA92 adheres to polystyrene film, suggesting involvement in degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 degrades polystyrene, contributing to the biodegradation of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is considered capable of degrading polystyrene based on its activity in experiments&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is involved in the degradation of polystyrene, contributing to its biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 is studied for its potential role in the biodegradation of polystyrene, given its growth characteristics.&lt;SEP&gt;A. tumefaciens MA92 showed high adhesion to polystyrene films but unclear degradation ability due to excessive bacterial growth.</data>
