    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="P. NITROREDUCENS MA77">
      <data key="d3">52.0</data>
      <data key="d4">P. nitroreducens MA77 adheres to polystyrene film, indicating potential for biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 degrades polystyrene, aiding in the breakdown of plastic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is capable of degrading polystyrene under specific conditions, aiding in its environmental breakdown.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 is evaluated for its ability to degrade polystyrene, as part of research on biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 reduced the size and number of polystyrene particles, indicating its role in degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;P. nitroreducens MA77 shows consistent polystyrene-degrading activity through surface destruction and decomposition of polystyrene particles</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
