    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="STARVATION">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polystyrene (PS) is an insufficient food source for mealworms, leading to starvation-like conditions that affect their growth and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;Polystyrene is an insufficient diet for Tenebrio molitor larvae, leading to starvation and physiological responses such as decreased reserve density.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLYSTYRENE" target="PS LARGE GROUP">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The PS large group is used to study the effects of large amounts of polystyrene on the survival and energy dynamics of Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </edge>
