      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLYETHYLENE" target="BACILLUS SP. YP1">
      <data key="d3">173.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacillus sp. YP1 degrades polyethylene, contributing to the biodegradation of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is capable of degrading polyethylene, demonstrating the role of gut bacteria in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is more efficient in degrading LDPE films compared to other bacterial isolates.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain that can degrade polyethylene, isolated from the gut of plastic-eating waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, isolated from the gut of waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, highlighting its role in the biodegradation of synthetic plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste reduction.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, demonstrating the role of gut bacteria in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is capable of degrading polyethylene, highlighting the role of gut bacteria in plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, a related plastic material.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, demonstrating the role of gut bacteria in plastic degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, contributing to plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. strain YP1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterium isolated from waxworm guts, contributing to plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, isolated from the guts of plastic-eating waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polyethylene, isolated from waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is a polyethylene-degrading bacterial strain, providing a reference for plastic-degrading bacteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus sp. YP1 is involved in the degradation of polyethylene, demonstrating the role of bacteria in plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">6&lt;SEP&gt;7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0462cccaa75cf13e553e16026939880b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47</data>
    </edge>
