 plastic-eating waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 is another bacterial strain involved in polyethylene degradation, isolated from waxworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter asburiae VT1 contributes to the degradation of polyethylene, highlighting the role of gut bacteria in plastic waste management.</data>
