      <data key="d3">32.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter sp. D1 can biodegrade polyethylene, reducing plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain that can biodegrade polyethylene, indicating its role in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1, isolated from Galleria mellonella, is capable of biodegrading polyethylene.&lt;SEP&gt;Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterial strain that can degrade polyethylene, indicating its potential in plastic biodegradation</data>
