      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics can be fragmented into nanoplastics during digestion by organisms like Antarctic krill.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROPLASTIC" target="PLASTIC WASTE POLLUTION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics are a significant component of plastic waste pollution, resulting from the degradation of larger plastic items.</data>
