    <edge source="TENEBRIO OBSCURUS" target="LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE">
      <data key="d3">40.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio obscurus can biodegrade low-density polyethylene independently of gut microbes, highlighting its unique biodegradation capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio obscurus can biodegrade low-density polyethylene, demonstrating its potential in plastic waste management.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio obscurus has been confirmed to biodegrade low-density polyethylene, even in the absence of gut microbes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio obscurus larvae can biodegrade low-density polyethylene through gut-microbe-independent depolymerization.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO OBSCURUS" target="CORN FLOUR">
      <data key="d3">36.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Corn flour enhances the consumption and biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by Tenebrio obscurus larvae, improving their survival and growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour enhances the plastic consumption rate of Tenebrio obscurus, improving their ability to degrade plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour is the normal diet for Tenebrio obscurus larvae, providing essential nutrients for their growth and PS biodegradation&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour is used as a codiet in feeding experiments with Tenebrio obscurus to study its effect on polystyrene degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Corn flour supplementation increases the polystyrene consumption rate of Tenebrio obscurus larvae</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO OBSCURUS" target="LDPE">
      <data key="d3">162.0</data>
      <data key="d4">**Tenebrio obscurus** larvae, a species closely related to **Tenebrio molitor**, have demonstrated a significant ability to biodegrade **low-density polyethylene (LDPE)**, a common type of plastic. These larvae consume LDPE, leading to changes in their gut microbial community, which aids in the biodegradation process. The larvae are capable of breaking down LDPE through broad depolymerization, significantly reducing its molecular weight and altering its hydrophobicity. This process contributes to the reduction of environmental pollution and plastic waste, particularly in the form of microplastics.

Studies indicate that **Tenebrio obscurus** larvae show a higher efficiency in biodegrading LDPE compared to other types of polyethylene, such as **HDPE** and **LLDPE**. The larvae adapt their gut microbiota to survive on plastic-based diets, which results in oxidative stress and changes in the composition of their gut microbiome. While **Tenebrio obscurus** larvae can also consume and biodegrade LDPE foams, their efficiency in doing so is slightly lower compared to **Tenebrio molitor**. However, they exhibit higher digestibility of LDPE, suggesting greater overall efficiency in the biodegradation process.

In summary, **Tenebrio obscurus** larvae play a crucial role in the biodegradation of LDPE, demonstrating capabilities similar to **Tenebrio molitor** but with some variations in efficiency and adaptability. Their ability to degrade LDPE contributes to the reduction of plastic waste and environmental pollution, making them a valuable subject of study in the field of plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae</data>
    </edge>
