    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROPLASTICS" target="GREATER WAX MOTH">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Greater wax moth larvae can completely digest and biodegrade polystyrene microplastics, offering a potential solution for plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROPLASTICS" target="EISENIA FETIDA">
      <data key="d3">40.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Earthworms are negatively affected by microplastics, which can damage their reproductive and immune systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida is used to study the bioaccumulation of hazardous organic compounds from microplastics in soil&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida (earthworms) experience oxidative damage and lipid peroxidation when exposed to microplastics, similar to mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida can disintegrate PLA microplastics into sub-micron particles in their digestive tracts, highlighting their role in plastic biofragmentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida is used to study the combined effects of microplastics and chemicals like atrazine on oxidative stress and gene expression.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MICROPLASTICS" target="OXIDATIVE STRESS">
      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics can activate oxidative stress pathways, leading to cellular damage in organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics induce oxidative stress in organisms, leading to tissue damage and toxic effects.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is induced in Tenebrio larvae due to the ingestion and biodegradation of polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Microplastics can induce oxidative stress in organisms, leading to cellular damage and inflammatory responses.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628</data>
    </edge>
