    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="OXIDATIVE STRESS">
      <data key="d3">56.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworm larvae experience oxidative stress when exposed to polyethylene microplastics, indicated by increased reactive oxygen species and antioxidant enzyme activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is induced in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of PE.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress is measured in mealworm larvae through ROS, MDA, and antioxidant enzyme levels during plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The biodegradation of PE by mealworm larvae leads to oxidative stress, characterized by increased ROS and MDA levels.&lt;SEP&gt;The biodegradation of PE microplastics by mealworm larvae induces oxidative stress, leading to physiological damage.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress may result from the degradation of oxo-degradable polyethylene in the digestive system of mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="RESIDUAL MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mealworm larvae excrete residual microplastics in their frass after biodegrading polyethylene, indicating incomplete digestion of the plastic.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="1,2,4-TRICHLOROBENZENE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">1,2,4-Trichlorobenzene is used in experiments to measure the biodegradation of polyethylene (PE) by mealworm larvae</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="FOOD-GRADE JELLY">
      <data key="d3">6.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Food-grade jelly is used to create a mixture of polyethylene (PE) and bran for feeding mealworm larvae in biodegradation studies</data>
      <data key="d5">6</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60</data>
    </edge>
