      <data key="d6">chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="ADULT BEETLES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Adult beetles are the final developmental stage of mealworms and can also eat plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="GUT-ASSOCIATED BACTERIA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut-associated bacteria in mealworm larvae play a crucial role in the degradation of plastics and other materials.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ff1127258b5df378d8b32fff2a93eb84</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MEALWORM LARVAE" target="DIET 2">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Diet 2, which includes water, improves the growth and PS consumption rates of mealworm larvae compared to other diets.</data>
