    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Reactive oxygen species (ROS) are responsible for inducing oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species contribute to oxidative stress in mealworm larvae exposed to polyethylene microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="ANTIOXIDANT ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Antioxidant enzymes help mitigate oxidative stress in mealworm larvae by neutralizing reactive oxygen species.&lt;SEP&gt;Antioxidant enzymes, such as SOD, GST, and CAD, counteract oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative stress triggers the activation of antioxidant enzymes, such as SOD, GST, and CAT, to neutralize reactive oxygen species (ROS).</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="LIPID PEROXIDATION">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lipid peroxidation is a consequence of oxidative stress, causing cellular damage in mealworm larvae during PE biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipid peroxidation is a consequence of oxidative stress, leading to cell damage in mealworm larvae exposed to polyethylene microplastics.&lt;SEP&gt;Lipid peroxidation is a marker of oxidative stress, indicating damage to cell membranes caused by reactive oxygen species (ROS).</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Physiological responses in mealworm larvae include oxidative stress when exposed to polyethylene microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="POLYETHYLENE (PE) MICROPLASTICS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The ingestion and biodegradation of PE microplastics by mealworm larvae trigger oxidative stress, leading to physiological damage.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="SOD">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">SOD is an antioxidant enzyme that mitigates oxidative stress in Tenebrio larvae caused by PE-MPs.&lt;SEP&gt;SOD scavenges free radicals to protect mealworm larvae from oxidative stress during PE biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="CAT">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">CAT mitigates oxidative stress by breaking down hydrogen peroxide during PE biodegradation in mealworm larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="REACTIVE OXYGEN SPECIES (ROS)">
      <data key="d3">18.0</data>
      <data key="d4">ROS generation during PE biodegradation leads to oxidative stress and damage in mealworm larvae.&lt;SEP&gt;Reactive oxygen species (ROS) are key contributors to oxidative stress in organisms exposed to microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="ANTIOXIDANT SYSTEMS">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Antioxidant systems in mealworms are damaged due to oxidative stress caused by ultrahigh-MW polystyrene polymers.&lt;SEP&gt;Antioxidant systems in mealworms are impacted by oxidative stress during polystyrene biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Antioxidant systems, including SOD, GST, and CAT, are triggered to mitigate oxidative stress during PE biodegradation in mealworm larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="EISENIA FETIDA">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Eisenia fetida exposed to PS MPs showed increased ROS levels, indicating oxidative stress.&lt;SEP&gt;Eisenia fetida is used to study oxidative stress caused by exposure to microplastics and chemicals like atrazine.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="GUT CELLS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut cells were studied to evaluate oxidative stress parameters in insects fed with polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="T. MOLITOR">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Oxidative stress levels in T. molitor gut cells are measured to assess the impact of Styrofoam consumption.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATIVE STRESS" target="Z. MORIO">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Oxidative stress levels in Z. morio gut cells are measured to assess the impact of Styrofoam consumption.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb</data>
    </edge>
