      <data key="d6">chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d3">35.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Superworms are being studied for their ability to chew, degrade, and mineralize Styrofoam as a sole diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms consume and degrade Styrofoam, contributing to its biodegradation and mineralization into CO2.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms consume and degrade Styrofoam, contributing to its biodegradation and reducing environmental pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Superworms consume and degrade Styrofoam, supporting their survival and development into adult beetles.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="GUT MICROBIAL SYMBIONTS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gut microbial symbionts in superworms are hypothesized to play a key role in the biodegradation of Styrofoam.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="GENTAMICIN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gentamicin suppresses the gut bacteria of superworms, negatively impacting their ability to degrade Styrofoam.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="RIFAMPICIN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Rifampicin, in combination with other antibiotics, suppresses gut bacteria in superworms, affecting their ability to degrade Styrofoam.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="STREPTOMYCIN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Streptomycin, in combination with other antibiotics, suppresses gut bacteria in superworms, affecting their ability to degrade Styrofoam.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="CARBON DIOXIDE (CO2)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Superworms contribute to the mineralization of Styrofoam into CO2 during the biodegradation process.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="OXIDATIVE DEGRADATION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Superworms facilitate the oxidative degradation of polyethylene in their gut, contributing to plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SUPERWORMS" target="GUT MICROBIOME CHANGES">
