      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Scanning electron microphotography is used to analyze the surface structure of polystyrene (PS) before and after degradation by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS" target="FOOD ADDITIVES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Food additives like wheat bran and corn flour are used to enhance the degradation efficiency of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS" target="LARVAE">
      <data key="d3">38.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Larvae can degrade polystyrene (PS), with removal efficiencies influenced by the presence of bran in their diet.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae were exposed to PS to assess its biodegradation and impact on metabolism.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae were fed with PS to assess its effects on ROS levels, showing similar ROS levels to those fed with bran only.&lt;SEP&gt;Larvae were fed polystyrene (PS) to study its effects on their growth and development, contributing to research on biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS" target="HAFNIA-OBSUMBACTER SP.">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Hafnia-Obsumbacter sp. is associated with the degradation of PS in Zophobas atratus larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS" target="TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PS microplastics, though ingestion leads to oxidative stress and physiological damage, less severe than PVC.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS" target="STYROFOAM">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polystyrene (PS) is the primary component of Styrofoam, used in the study to assess its biodegradation potential by larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </edge>
