    <edge source="SYMBIOTIC BACTERIA" target="NITROGENASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Symbiotic bacteria produce nitrogenase, which is essential for nitrogen fixation in nutrient-deficient environments.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYMBIOTIC BACTERIA" target="NITROGEN FIXATION">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Symbiotic bacteria in the guts of insects like termites and beetles play a key role in nitrogen fixation, converting atmospheric nitrogen into usable forms.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="SYMBIOTIC BACTERIA" target="TERMITES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Termites host symbiotic bacteria in their guts that aid in nitrogen fixation and cellulose degradation, essential for their survival and ecosystem functioning.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1</data>
    </edge>
