    </edge>
    <edge source="ORGANIC PHOSPHORUS COMPOUNDS" target="INORGANIC SOLUBLE PHOSPHATES">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Organic phosphorus compounds are transformed into inorganic soluble phosphates by enzymes in the digestive tracts of mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NITROGEN FIXATION" target="PET">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Nitrogen fixation by gut microbes provides limited nitrogen to Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with PET.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation by gut microbes provides limited nitrogen to Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with PET.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation supports enzyme synthesis and PET digestion in Tenebrio molitor larvae by converting N2 into amino acids.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen fixation supports enzyme synthesis and PET digestion in Tenebrio molitor larvae by converting N2 into amino acids.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NITROGEN FIXATION" target="NITROGEN-FIXING BACTERIA">
      <data key="d3">43.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae carry out nitrogen fixation, providing a limited source of nitrogen when the larvae are fed plastic-only diets.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-fixing bacteria play a crucial role in the nitrogen fixation process, particularly in the guts of termites and other insects.&lt;SEP&gt;Nitrogen-fixing bacteria, such as Klebsiella, are essential for nitrogen fixation in mealworms, enabling them to survive on nitrogen-deficient plastic diets.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aac53ba8b358857c4dcd3b6cd9e8991</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NITROGEN FIXATION" target="PANTOEE SP.">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Pantoee sp. is involved in nitrogen fixation and increases amino acid content in plant tissues, supporting plant growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Pantoee sp. is involved in nitrogen fixation and increases amino acid content in plant tissues, supporting plant growth.&lt;SEP&gt;Pantoee sp. is involved in nitrogen fixation, converting atmospheric nitrogen into forms usable by plants.&lt;SEP&gt;Pantoee sp. is involved in nitrogen fixation, converting atmospheric nitrogen into forms usable by plants.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NITROGEN FIXATION" target="KLEBSIELLA">
      <data key="d3">17.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Klebsiella bacteria in the gut of mealworms contribute to nitrogen fixation.&lt;SEP&gt;Klebsiella, a gut bacterium in mealworms, is involved in nitrogen fixation, helping mealworms overcome nitrogen deficiency in plastic diets.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8</data>
    </edge>
