    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE" target="MICROPLASTICS (MPS)">
      <data key="d3">25.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Microplastics induce negative physiological responses in Tenebrio molitor larvae, such as dehydration, malnutrition, and growth inhibition, depending on the type of plastic.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of consuming and degrading microplastics (MPs), offering a potential solution to microplastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor larvae ingest microplastics, which affects their growth and survival rates, with higher intake leading to more adverse effects.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE" target="PVC">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PVC microplastics, but ingestion causes significant oxidative stress and physiological damage.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE" target="PLA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tenebrio molitor larvae can biodegrade PLA microplastics with the least oxidative stress and physiological damage compared to PVC and PS.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </edge>
