      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Greater wax moth larvae have been observed to degrade LDPE films, creating holes and causing mass loss in the plastic substrate.&lt;SEP&gt;The greater wax moth can digest low-density polyethylene films, contributing to research on plastic waste biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;The greater wax moth larvae can chew and degrade LDPE, contributing to its biodegradation</data>
