    <edge source="PUPATION" target="REPRODUCTION BUFFER">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Pupation in Tenebrio molitor larvae depends on the filling of the reproduction buffer, which is influenced by their diet and energy reserves.&lt;SEP&gt;The reproduction buffer influences the timing of pupation in larvae, as it represents the energy allocated for reproduction.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LARVAL FRASS" target="OPTICAL MICROSCOPE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Larval frass is analyzed using an optical microscope to observe residual plastics and assess degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="EPS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">EPS shows signs of oxidation during biodegradation by mealworms, with new carbonyl and hydroxyl groups detected</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="FTIR SPECTRA">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">FTIR spectra show chemical modifications, such as hydroxyl groups and C—N stretch vibrations, indicating oxidation of microplastics</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="HYDROXYL GROUPS">
      <data key="d3">23.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Hydroxyl groups (C-OH) appear on the surface of polystyrene films during biodegradation, indicating oxidation and chemical changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyl groups in FTIR spectra provide evidence of oxidation in microplastics after ingestion by mealworms&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidation during PP biodegradation results in the formation of hydroxyl groups (O-H), as detected in FTIR spectra.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="C—N STRETCH VIBRATION">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">C—N stretch vibration in FTIR spectra indicates nitrogen-related oxidation in microplastics</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="CARBON-OXYGEN BONDS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Carbon-oxygen bonds (C-O) are formed on the surface of polystyrene films during biodegradation, providing evidence of oxidation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="OXIDATION" target="ATR-FTIR ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">ATR-FTIR analysis confirmed the occurrence of oxidation in mask layers after passing through the guts of yellow mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </edge>
