    <edge source="ACHROIA GRISELLA" target="POLYETHYLENE (HDPE)">
      <data key="d3">43.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Achroia grisella (lesser waxworm) is capable of biodegrading high-density polyethylene (HDPE), contributing to the reduction of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Achroia grisella can efficiently biodegrade polyethylene (HDPE) waste, offering a potential solution for plastic pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Achroia grisella, the lesser waxmoth, is capable of biodegrading polyethylene (HDPE) waste, offering a potential solution to plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d5">8&lt;SEP&gt;9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACHROIA GRISELLA" target="PE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Achroia grisella larvae can biodegrade polyethylene (PE), demonstrating their role in plastic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ACHROIA GRISELLA" target="WAX COMB">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Supplementing the diet of lesser waxworms with wax comb enhances the biodegradation of polyethylene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c</data>
