    <edge source="PET" target="ALKANE 1-MONOOXYGENASE">
      <data key="d3">28.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Alkane 1-monoxygenase can potentially degrade PET by breaking down hydrocarbon bonds, although direct evidence for PET degradation is not yet established.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane 1-monoxygenase can potentially degrade PET by breaking down hydrocarbon bonds, although direct evidence for PET degradation is not yet established.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane 1-monoxygenase introduces oxygen to alkane substrates, breaking down hydrocarbons and contributing to PET degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Alkane 1-monoxygenase introduces oxygen to alkane substrates, breaking down hydrocarbons and contributing to PET degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
