      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MORPHOLOGICAL PARAMETERS" target="WEIGHT CHANGES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Morphological parameters, such as weight changes, are observed in mealworm larvae when fed with different types of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PLASTIC UTILIZATION" target="STUDENT T-TEST">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Student t-test was used to determine significant differences in the mass reduction of plastics consumed by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PLASTIC UTILIZATION" target="ANOVA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">ANOVA with post hoc Tukey's test was used to analyze significant differences between the degradation rates of different plastics by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOVA" target="TURBIDITY ASSAY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">ANOVA is used to statistically evaluate differences in turbidity assay results, indicating bacterial growth or degradation activity</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANOVA" target="TUKEY'S CORRECTION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tukey's correction is applied to ANOVA tests to adjust p-values for multiple comparisons.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="POLYURETHANE (PU1)" target="ELEMENTS CONTENT ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Polyurethane (PU1) was studied for its elemental content, showing high concentrations of Ca, Al, Si, and Cl, which are relevant for its environmental behavior.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-065b846c5f5f23f64023995cdb21c3db</data>
    </edge>
