      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Potassium bromide (KBr) is used to prepare samples for Fourier-transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) analysis.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WORMS" target="URBAN FARMING">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Urban farming utilizes worms for plastic waste degradation and their frass for supporting food crop growth, contributing to sustainability.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WORMS" target="FOOD CROPS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Worm frass supports the growth of food crops, making worms a dual solution for plastic waste reduction and food production.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WORMS" target="INDOOR IMPLEMENTATION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Worm-based plastic degradation and frass-supported plant growth can be implemented indoors, making it a scalable urban solution.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WORMS" target="FOOD SUSTAINABILITY">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Worms contribute to food sustainability by serving as an alternative protein source and producing frass that supports food crop growth.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BLACK SOLDIER FLY FRASS" target="NITROGEN FERTILIZER EQUIVALENCE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Black soldier fly frass has nitrogen fertilizer equivalence, making it an effective biofertilizer for crop production.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c</data>
    </edge>
