    <edge source="CO2 PRODUCTION" target="SERUM BOTTLE ASSAYS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Serum bottle assays are used to measure CO2 production, indicating the mineralization of polystyrene by PS-degrading bacteria.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-cc75b7e672a7f7c036713dfa2675d79a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CO2 PRODUCTION" target="SERUM BOTTLES">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Serum bottles are used to measure CO2 production during microbial respiration, indicating the extent of plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Serum bottles are used to measure CO2 production during the biodegradation of polystyrene by the gut microbiome.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CO2 PRODUCTION" target="MICROBIAL ENRICHMENT">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The microbial enrichment produces higher levels of CO2 during the biodegradation of polystyrene, indicating more efficient mineralization.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS FILM" target="MICROBIAL ENRICHMENT">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PS film is used as a carbon source in experiments with microbial enrichment to study enhanced biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba</data>
    </edge>
