      <data key="d6">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GWP" target="BIODIESEL">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Global Warming Potential (GWP) is used to estimate the environmental impact of producing biodiesel from mealworm lipids</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODIESEL" target="SCUM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Scum from wastewater treatment facilities can be processed into biodiesel, contributing to waste valorization and renewable energy production.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODIESEL" target="LOW S DIESEL">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodiesel produced from mealworm remains and other waste materials can offset the use of low S diesel, reducing environmental impact.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODIESEL" target="LOW S DIESEL OFFSET">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biodiesel produced from waste materials offsets the use of low S diesel, reducing greenhouse gas emissions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODIESEL" target="FATTY ACID METHYL ESTERS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fatty acid methyl esters are derived from mealworm grease and explored as a potential feedstock for biodiesel production.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MIXED PLASTIC WASTE" target="MONTE CARLO SIMULATION">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Monte Carlo simulation is used to estimate the variability and uncertainty in treating mixed plastic waste, including energy, cost, and environmental metrics.</data>
