    </edge>
    <edge source="PACKAGING FILMS" target="GERHARDT AND LINDGREN">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Gerhardt and Lindgren tested the resistance of packaging films to penetration by stored-product insects.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GC-TOF-MS" target="METABOLOMICS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Metabolomics analysis using GC-TOF-MS was performed to study the metabolic profiles of mealworm larvae during PS biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GC-TOF-MS" target="MYRISTIC ACID-D27">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Myristic acid-d27 is used as an internal standard in the GC-TOF-MS analysis to quantify metabolites.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GC-TOF-MS" target="AGILENT TECHNOLOGIES 7200 ACCURATE-MASS Q-TOF">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Agilent Technologies 7200 Accurate-Mass Q-ToF is part of the GC-TOF-MS system used for metabolite analysis.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="GC-TOF-MS" target="METABOLIC PROFILING">
      <data key="d3">16.0</data>
      <data key="d4">GC-TOF-MS is a technique used for metabolic profiling in studies of plastic biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Metabolic profiling using GC-TOF-MS is used to evaluate the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METABOLOMICS" target="BREAST CANCER MICE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Metabolomics is used to study the impact of polybrominated diphenyl ether-47 on breast cancer mice.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="BIT-26">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fatty acid profiles were used as chemotaxonomic markers to characterize BIT-26 and differentiate it from other Mixta species.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="BIT-26T">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fatty acids were analyzed to characterize the chemical composition of BIT-26T, providing insights into its metabolic profile.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="STRAIN BIT-26T">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The fatty acid composition of strain BIT-26T was analyzed to determine its chemotaxonomic profile and distinguish it from related species.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="MIXTA TENEBRIONIS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fatty acids are used to characterize Mixta tenebrionis, providing insights into its biochemical properties.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="FEED">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Fatty acids are analyzed to determine the nutritional impact of different feed types on Tenebrio molitor larvae.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="DRIED WHEY">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Dried whey contributes to the fatty acid content in larvae, as measured in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Dried whey is analyzed for its fatty acid composition, revealing higher proportions of certain fatty acids compared to polystyrene and potatoes.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="FOOD AND AGRICULTURE ORGANIZATION (FAO)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The FAO provides guidelines on fatty acid ratios, which are used to assess the nutritional suitability of mealworm larvae as a food source.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="POTATOES">
      <data key="d3">15.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Potatoes are analyzed for their fatty acid composition, showing lower proportions of polyenoic fatty acids compared to dried whey and polystyrene.&lt;SEP&gt;Potatoes as feed affect the fatty acid profile of mealworm larvae, with a notable content of saturated and monoenoic fatty acids.</data>
      <data key="d5">7&lt;SEP&gt;8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb542a26376f51c3cd9247fe3d56854</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FATTY ACIDS" target="WHEY">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Whey as feed influences the fatty acid content of mealworm larvae, particularly increasing monoenoic fatty acids.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84</data>
    </edge>
