      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 demonstrates the ability to degrade polystyrene under anaerobic conditions, a novel finding in plastic biodegradation research.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3" target="LIPID A">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Lipid A is upregulated in Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 during polystyrene biodegradation, indicating changes in cellular metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3" target="BIOFILM-ASSOCIATED PROTEINS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Biofilm-associated proteins are upregulated in Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 during polystyrene biodegradation, facilitating the degradation process.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627</data>
    </edge>
