    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3" target="CELL VIABILITY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Cell viability is measured to assess the health of Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 during polystyrene (PS) degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3" target="MI-PS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter hormaechei LG3 shows high anaerobic PS-degrading activity, including the degradation of Mi-PS.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI LG3" target="BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 exhibits higher anaerobic PS-degrading activity compared to SCGB1, highlighting differences in biodegradation capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1" target="PS FILMS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">PS films are used in studies to assess the biodegradation capabilities of Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1" target="AEROBIC CONDITIONS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 degrades polystyrene (PS) under aerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANAEROBIC BIODEGRADATION" target="ENTEROBACTER SPP.">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter spp. play a significant role in the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene in mealworm gut microbiota.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ANAEROBIC BIODEGRADATION" target="LG3">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 performs anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene, involving oxidation and depolymerization stages.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PS EMULSION" target="FILTER PAPER">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Filter paper is used to filter and measure the weight of PS particles in the emulsion.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fdb13eda4d3cf5385a0a8284c7e213b0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AEROBIC CONDITIONS" target="ENTEROBACTER GENUS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacterial strains from the Enterobacter genus are also tested for polystyrene degradation under aerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AEROBIC CONDITIONS" target="STRAIN SCGB1">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain SCGB1 degrades polystyrene effectively under aerobic conditions but shows no significant activity under anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="AEROBIC CONDITIONS" target="B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 produces specific metabolites during the aerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="L-CYSTEINE HYDROCHLORIDE" target="FUNGAL MINIMUM MEDIUM (FMM)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">L-cysteine hydrochloride is added to FMM to enhance anaerobic conditions for microbial cultivation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fdb13eda4d3cf5385a0a8284c7e213b0</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PALLADIUM CATALYST" target="OXYGEN (O₂)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">A palladium catalyst is used to remove traces of oxygen (O₂) from the chamber's atmosphere by reacting with hydrogen (H₂).</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PALLADIUM CATALYST" target="HYDROGEN (H₂)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Hydrogen (H₂) is used with a palladium catalyst to remove traces of oxygen (O₂) from the chamber's atmosphere.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="HYDROGEN SULFIDE REMOVAL COLUMN" target="HYDROGEN SULFIDE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Hydrogen sulfide is removed from the chamber's atmosphere by continuously recirculating it through a hydrogen sulfide removal column.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BIODEGRADATION ASSAY" target="SOLID-PHASE MICROEXTRACTION GAS CHROMATOGRAPHY (SPME/GC—MS)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Solid-phase microextraction gas chromatography (SPME/GC—MS) is used for mass spectrometry analysis in biodegradation studies.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FMM AGAR PLATES" target="16 S RRNA GENE SEQUENCING">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacteria forming clear zones on FMM agar plates are identified using 16 S rRNA gene sequencing.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FMM AGAR PLATES" target="STRAIN LG3">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain LG3 is cultured on FMM agar plates to study its ability to degrade polystyrene under various conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FMM AGAR PLATES" target="STRAIN SCGB1">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain SCGB1 is cultured on FMM agar plates to assess its polystyrene-degrading capabilities under aerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="16 S RRNA GENE SEQUENCING" target="BLAST DATABASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">16 S rRNA gene sequences are aligned and compared using the BLAST database for phylogenetic analysis.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="NEIGHBOR-JOINING METHOD" target="KIMURA TWO-PARAMETER MODEL">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The neighbor-joining method and Kimura two-parameter model are used together to construct evolutionary trees based on 16 S rRNA gene sequences.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="FMM">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS is added to FMM medium to study bacterial degradation under controlled conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="STRAIN LG3">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain LG3 is studied for its potential to degrade Mi-PS, indicating its role in microplastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="CH4">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS degradation by bacteria can lead to the production of CH4, a byproduct of anaerobic degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="E. HORMAECHEI LG3">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">E. hormaechei LG3 effectively degrades Mi-PS, a microplastic form of polystyrene, under anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="FE-SEM">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">FE-SEM is used to visualize the morphological changes in Mi-PS during biodegradation by bacterial strains like E. hormaechei LG3.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="SPME/GC-MS ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">SPME/GC-MS analysis is used to identify hydroxyl compounds produced during the biodegradation of Mi-PS.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="ALIPHATIC AND AROMATIC ALCOHOLS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Aliphatic and aromatic alcohols are compounds identified during the biodegradation of Mi-PS, indicating the breakdown of the polymer.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="ENTEROBACTER LG3">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter LG3 effectively degrades Mi-PS under both aerobic and anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 degrades Mi-PS but shows reduced activity under anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="FE-SEM IMAGE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">FE-SEM imaging is used to visualize the physical changes in Mi-PS during biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="EXIGUOBACTERIUM STRAIN YT2">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Exiguobacterium strain YT2 is studied for its ability to degrade Mi-PS, contributing to the understanding of plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="PEROXIREDOXIN FAMILY ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS treatment affects the expression levels of peroxiredoxin family enzymes, indicating oxidative stress response.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="LIPID A SYNTHESIS PATHWAY PROTEINS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS treatment alters the expression of lipid A synthesis pathway proteins, suggesting changes in lipopolysaccharide biosynthesis.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="FLAGELLAR-ASSOCIATED PROTEINS">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS treatment influences the expression of flagellar-associated proteins, impacting bacterial motility.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MI-PS" target="GLYCOLYSIS PATHWAY ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Mi-PS treatment affects the expression of glycolysis pathway enzymes, indicating changes in energy metabolism.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STRAIN LG3" target="WHOLE GENOME SEQUENCE ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Whole genome sequence analysis is performed on Strain LG3 to understand its genetic capabilities in degrading microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STRAIN LG3" target="SW">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">SW is used as a medium for resuspending Strain LG3 cell suspensions in the study.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STRAIN LG3" target="HIGENE™ GENOMIC DNA PREP KIT">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The HiGene™ Genomic DNA Prep Kit is used to extract genomic DNA from Strain LG3 for whole genome sequencing.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STRAIN LG3" target="WEIGHT REDUCTION">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain LG3 causes significant weight reduction in polystyrene films under both aerobic and anaerobic conditions, indicating its biodegradation capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="STRAIN LG3" target="CFU CONCENTRATION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Strain LG3 exhibits high CFU concentrations when utilizing polystyrene as a carbon source, particularly under aerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WHOLE GENOME SEQUENCE ANALYSIS" target="OXFORD NANOPORE TECHNOLOGIES (ONT)">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">ONT provides protocols and tools for whole genome sequencing, used in the analysis of Strain LG3.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WHOLE GENOME SEQUENCE ANALYSIS" target="FLYE ASSEMBLER">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The Flye assembler is used to assemble whole genome sequences from sequencing reads of Strain LG3.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WHOLE GENOME SEQUENCE ANALYSIS" target="PROKKA">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
