      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">E. hormaechei LG3 exhibits more effective depolymerization of polystyrene compared to B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="E. HORMAECHEI LG3" target="NANOPORE SEQUENCING">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Nanopore sequencing is used to analyze the genome of E. hormaechei LG3, identifying key enzymes involved in polystyrene biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="E. HORMAECHEI LG3" target="LIPID A SYNTHESIS PATHWAY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The lipid A synthesis pathway is upregulated in E. hormaechei LG3 during the biodegradation of polystyrene, indicating metabolic changes.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="E. HORMAECHEI LG3" target="FLAGELLAR PROTEIN-CODING GENES">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Flagellar protein-coding genes are downregulated in E. hormaechei LG3 during the biodegradation of polystyrene, suggesting reduced motility.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="E. HORMAECHEI LG3" target="GLYCOLYTIC PATHWAY">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">The glycolytic pathway is downregulated in E. hormaechei LG3 during the biodegradation of polystyrene, indicating metabolic shifts.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1" target="AEROBIC RESPIRATION">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 uses aerobic respiration to degrade polystyrene in the presence of oxygen.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1" target="ISOBUTYRIC ACID">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Isobutyric acid is a specific metabolite produced by B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 during the aerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="B. AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCGB1" target="ISOVALERIC ACID">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Isovaleric acid is a specific metabolite produced by B. amyloliquefaciens SCGB1 during the aerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="WCA VALUES" target="OXIDIZED PS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">WCA values are used to assess changes in the hydrophobicity of oxidized PS during biodegradation.</data>
