      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER LG3" target="DENITRIFICATION ENZYMES">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Denitrification enzymes are expressed in Enterobacter LG3 during the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER LG3" target="METHYL 2-HYDROXYBENZOATE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Methyl 2-hydroxybenzoate is a secondary product of polystyrene degradation produced by Enterobacter LG3 under anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER LG3" target="PEROXIREDOXINS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Peroxiredoxins are upregulated in Enterobacter LG3 during the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER LG3" target="ANAEROBIC RESPIRATION">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter LG3 uses anaerobic respiration to degrade polystyrene under oxygen-limited conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER LG3" target="OXIDIZED PS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter LG3 effectively degrades oxidized PS into smaller molecules under anaerobic conditions.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="METHYL 2-HYDROXYBENZOATE" target="LG3">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 produces methyl 2-hydroxybenzoate as an intermediate during the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene, indicating shared mechanisms with styrene degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PEROXIREDOXINS" target="LG3">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 upregulates peroxiredoxins, enzymes that protect against oxidative stress, during the degradation of polystyrene microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="MICROPLASTICS (MI-PS)">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 degrades polystyrene microplastics (Mi-PS) under anaerobic conditions, altering its metabolic pathways and physiological activities.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="GUAIACOL PEROXIDASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 expresses guaiacol peroxidase, an enzyme involved in the oxidation of aryl alcohol compounds during polystyrene degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="POLYPHENOL OXIDASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 expresses polyphenol oxidase, an enzyme involved in the oxidation of aryl alcohol compounds during polystyrene degradation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="1,2-PHENYLACETYL-COA EPOXIDASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 expresses 1,2-phenylacetyl-CoA epoxidase, an enzyme involved in the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="2-OCTAPRENYLPHENOL HYDROXYLASE">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">LG3 expresses 2-octaprenylphenol hydroxylase, an enzyme involved in the anaerobic biodegradation of polystyrene.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LG3" target="RNA-SEQ ANALYSIS">
      <data key="d3">9.0</data>
      <data key="d4">RNA-seq analysis reveals changes in gene expression and metabolic pathways in LG3 during the degradation of polystyrene microplastics.</data>
      <data key="d5">9</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER AEROGENES" target="ISOBUTANOL">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter aerogenes utilizes formate and nitrate for the semi-anaerobic production of isobutanol, demonstrating its metabolic capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d5">7</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="BACILLUS AMYLOLIQUEFACIENS SCQ1" target="COLITIS">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Bacillus amyloliquefaciens SCQ1 alleviates dextran sulfate sodium-induced colitis in mice through immune regulation.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="LIMOSILACTOBACILLUS FERMENTUM JNUS32" target="PROBIOTIC">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Limosilactobacillus fermentum JNUS32 is a probiotic candidate with potential applications in functional food and feed supplements.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ENTEROBACTER ASBURIAE E7" target="AEROMONAS VERONII">
      <data key="d3">8.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Enterobacter asburiae E7 enhances resistance to Aeromonas veronii infection in common carp by stimulating the immune response.</data>
      <data key="d5">8</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CYPRINUS CARPIO" target="IMMUNE RESPONSE">
      <data key="d3">7.0</data>
